hadiths[981]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7119","Akhbarana Hushaym ibn Bashir, akhbarana Abdullah ibn Abi Salih Dhakwan from his father from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your oath is according to what your companion believes you upon."
"7120","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Mansur and Hisham from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The well is jubar, and the mine is jubar, and the beast is jubar, and in rikaz is the fifth."
"7121","Akhbarana Hushaym from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: Uyaynah ibn Hisn entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him kissing Hasan or Husayn, so he said to him: Do you kiss him, O Messenger of Allah; ten were born to me, I have kissed none of them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy shall not be shown mercy."
"7122","Haddathana Hushaym from Shubah from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah who said: He passed by people performing ablution and said: Complete the ablution, for I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"7123","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Abu Bishr from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my nation is the generation I was sent among, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; and Allah knows whether he said the third or not; then shall come a people who love fatness, testifying before they are asked to testify."
"7124","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad meaning Ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds the very property of his at a man who has gone bankrupt, he is more entitled to it than any other."
"7125","Haddathana Hushaym from Zakariyya from al-Shabi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a riding beast is mortgaged, upon the mortgagee is its fodder, and the milk of the milch beast is drunk, and upon him who drinks it is its upkeep, and he rides."
"7126","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarana Khalid from Yusuf or from his father Abdullah ibn al-Harith from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When they dispute over the road, seven cubits are taken from between them."
"7127","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Abu al-Juhaym al-Wasiti from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Imru al-Qays is the bearer of the banner of the poets to the Fire."
"7128","Haddathana Hushaym from Sayyar from Jabr ibn Ubaydah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised us the expedition of India; so if I am martyred I shall be of the best of martyrs, and if I return then I am Abu Hurayrah the freed."
"7129","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarana al-Awwam ibn Hawshab from Abdullah ibn al-Saib from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prescribed prayer to the prayer after it is expiation for what is between them. He said: And Friday to Friday, and the month to the month, meaning Ramadan to Ramadan, is expiation for what is between them. He said: Then he said after that: Except from three. He said: So I knew that matter was new: except from associating with Allah, and breaking the pledge, and abandoning the Sunnah. He said: As for breaking the pledge, that you pledge a man then go against him fighting him with your sword; and as for abandoning the Sunnah, leaving the community."
"7130","Haddathana Hushaym from Hisham from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The severity of heat is from the blast of Hell, so cool with the prayer."
"7131","Haddathana Hushaym from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The virgin is asked permission, and the previously married is consulted. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the virgin is shy. He said: Her silence is her consent."
"7132","Haddathana Hushaym from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trim the mustaches and leave the beards."
"7133","Haddathana Hushaym from Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah meaning from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), thus he said, that he forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"7134","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarana Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of Tashriq are days of food and remembrance of Allah. He said once: Days of eating and drinking."
"7135","Haddathana Hushaym who said: If I did not hear it from him meaning al-Zuhri, then haddathani Sufyan ibn Husayn from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No atirah in Islam and no fara."
"7136","Haddathana Hushaym from Sayyar from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs Hajj and does not utter obscenity nor commit sin returns as he was the day his mother bore him."
"7137","Haddathana Hushaym from Hisham from Ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah who said: Sulayman ibn Dawud said: I shall go around tonight upon a hundred women; every one of them shall bear a boy fighting in the path of Allah; and he did not make exception. So none bore except one of them, half a man. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he made exception, a hundred boys would have been born to him, all fighting in the path of Allah."
"7138","Haddathana Hushaym and Ismail ibn Ibrahim from Yunus from al-Hasan from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three; Hushaym said: So I shall not leave them till I die: Witr before sleep, and fasting three days of every month, and ghusl on Friday."
"7139","Haddathana Mutamir from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are of the fitrah: trimming the mustache, and clipping the nails, and plucking the armpit, and shaving the pubes, and circumcision."
"7140","Haddathana Mutamir ibn Sulayman, haddathana my father from Bakr from Abu Rafi who said: I prayed with Abu Hurayrah the Atamah prayer, or he said the Isha prayer, and he recited When the sky is split, and prostrated in it. So I said: O Abu Hurayrah. So he said: I prostrated in it behind Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I shall keep prostrating it till I meet him."
"7141","Haddathana Bishr ibn Mufaddal from Ibn Ajlan from Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the fly falls in the vessel of one of you, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure, and it shields with its wing in which is disease, so dip it all."
"7142","Haddathana Bishr from Ibn Ajlan from Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you reaches the gathering, let him greet; and when he wants to stand, let him greet; so the first is not more entitled than the last."
"7143","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Yusuf, haddathana Sufyan from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No child shall repay his father except that he finds him enslaved and buys him and frees him."
"7144","Haddathana Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The imam is only followed; so when he says takbir, say takbir; and when he bows, bow; and when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting all."
"7145","Haddathana Safwan ibn Isa, akhbarana Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind from Said al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is made a judge between people has been slaughtered without a knife."
"7146","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Shubah who said: I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do you know what backbiting is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Your mentioning your brother with what is not in him. He said: Have you seen, if in my brother is what I say to him, meaning. He said: If in him is what you say, then you have backbitten him; and if in him is not what you say, then you have slandered him."
"7147","Haddathana Ismail ibn Ibrahim, haddathana Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi and said takbir four times."
"7148","Haddathana Ismail, haddathana Ayyub from Abu Qilabah from Abu Hurayrah who said: When Ramadan came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ramadan has come to you, a blessed month; Allah has obligated its fasting upon you; in it the gates of Paradise are opened, and in it the gates of Hell are closed, and in it the devils are chained; in it is a night better than a thousand months; whoever is deprived its good has been deprived."
"7149","Haddathana Ismail, haddathana Ayyub from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man called to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Does one of us pray in one garment. He said: Do all of you find two garments."
"7150","Haddathana Ismail, haddathana Ayyub from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam and Ghifar and some of Muzaynah and Juhaynah, or some of Juhaynah and Muzaynah, are better with Allah, I think he said, on the Day of Resurrection, than Asad and Ghatafan and Hawazin and Tamim."
"7151","Haddathana Ismail, haddathana Ayyub from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Friday there is an hour no Muslim servant standing praying, asking Allah good, meets it but Allah gives it to him. And he gestured with his hand; we said: He makes it little, he deems it brief."
"7152","Haddathana Ismail, haddathana Ayyub from Muhammad who said: Either they boasted or they recalled: Are men more or women. So Abu Hurayrah said: Did not Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first group to enter Paradise is upon the form of the moon on the night of full moon, and the next upon the brightest brilliant star in the sky; for every man of them two wives, two, the marrow of their shins seen from behind the flesh; and in Paradise there is no unmarried."
"7153","Haddathana Ismail, akhbarana Ayyub from Ikrimah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. Ayyub said: So I was told a man drank from the mouth of a waterskin, and a snake came out."
"7154","Haddathana Ismail, haddathana Ayyub from Ikrimah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man shall prevent his neighbor from placing his timber, or he said a timber, in his wall."
"7155","Haddathana Yala ibn Ubayd, haddathana Abd al-Malik from Ata from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No charity except from sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"7156","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Zurah who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Khadijah; she has come to you with a vessel with food or drink in it; so when she comes to you, convey to her peace from her Lord and from me, and give her tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, no noise in it nor toil."
"7157","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has pledged for him who goes out in His path, going out only as jihad in My path and faith in Me and belief in My Messenger, that He shall admit him to Paradise or return him to the dwelling he went out from, attaining what he attained of reward or spoil. And by Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no wound is inflicted in the path of Allah but it shall come on the Day of Resurrection as it was the day it was inflicted, its color the color of blood and its scent the scent of musk. And by Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, were it not to burden the Muslims, I would never stay behind a detachment raiding in the path of Allah; but I do not find means so they follow me, nor are their souls content to stay behind me. And by Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I would love to raid in the path of Allah and be killed, then raid and be killed, then raid and be killed."
"7158","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten. He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten. He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: And those who shorten. He said: And those who shorten."
"7159","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which charity is greatest in reward. He said: By your father, you shall be told it: that you give while you are sound, miserly, fearing poverty and hoping for life; and do not delay till, when it reaches the throat, you say: For so-and-so such, and for so-and-so such, though it already belonged to so-and-so."
"7160","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Zurah who said: And I know it only from Abu Hurayrah who said: Jibril sat to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and looked to the sky, and behold an angel descending. So Jibril said: This angel has not descended since the day he was created before this hour. So when he descended he said: O Muhammad, your Lord has sent me to you. He said: Shall He make you a king prophet or a servant messenger. Jibril said: Be humble to your Lord, O Muhammad. He said: Rather a servant messenger."
"7161","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour shall not rise till the sun rises from its west; and when it rises and people see it, whoever is upon it shall believe; that is when no soul shall benefit from its faith that had not believed before or earned good in its faith."
"7162","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of uninterrupted fasting; he said it three times. They said: But you fast uninterrupted, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You are not in that like me; I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink; so undertake of deeds what you can bear."
"7163","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks people for their wealth in abundance only asks for embers, so let him take little of it or much."
"7164","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Umarah and Jarir from Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he said takbir in prayer would pause between the takbir and the recitation. So I said: May my father and mother be for you; have you seen your silence between the takbir and the recitation, tell me what it is. He said: I say: O Allah, distance me from my sins as You distanced between the east and the west; O Allah, cleanse me of my sins as the white garment of filth. Jarir said: As the garment is cleansed. O Allah, wash me of my sins with snow and water and hail. My father said: All of them from Abu Zurah except this, from Abu Salih."
"7165","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group to enter Paradise is upon the form of the moon on the night of full moon; then those after them upon the most intense light of a brilliant star in the sky; they do not urinate nor defecate nor spit nor blow their noses; their combs are gold, and their sweat is musk, and their censers are aloeswood, and their wives are houris; their natures upon the nature of one man, upon the form of their father Adam, sixty cubits tall."
"7166","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Zurah who said: I entered with Abu Hurayrah the house of Marwan ibn al-Hakam, and he saw in it images while it was being built. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: And who is more unjust than he who goes to create creation like My creation; let them create a grain, or let them create a seed, or let them create barley. Then he called for ablution and performed ablution and washed his forearms till he passed the elbows; and when he washed his feet he passed the ankles to the shins. So I said: What is this. So he said: This is the extent of the ornament."
"7167","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl from Umarah from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two words light on the tongue, heavy in the scale, beloved to the Merciful: Subhan Allah wa bihamdihi, Subhan Allah al-Azim."
"7168","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Asim ibn Kulayb from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen me, for Satan does not take my form. And Ibn Fudayl said once: Appear as me. For the true righteous dream of the believing servant is a part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"7169","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana al-Amash from a man from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the caller is entrusted; O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers."
"7170","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Yahya meaning Ibn Said from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and reckoning shall be forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"7171","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana my father from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wheat for wheat, and barley for barley, and dates for dates, and salt for salt, measure for measure and weight for weight; so whoever adds or seeks addition has taken usury, except what differs in kinds."
"7172","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer has a first and a last; and the first time of Zuhr is when the sun declines, and the last of its time is when the time of Asr enters; and the first time of Asr is when its time enters, and the last of its time is when the sun yellows; and the first time of Maghrib is when the sun sets, and the last of its time is when the horizon disappears; and the first time of Isha the last is when the horizon disappears, and the last of its time is when the night halves; and the first time of Fajr is when dawn rises, and the last of its time is when the sun rises."
"7173","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana my father from Umarah ibn al-Qaqa from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make the provision of the household of Muhammad sustenance."
"7174","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Dirar, and he is Abu Sinan, from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it; the fasting one has two joys: when he breaks he rejoices, and when he meets Allah and He rewards him he rejoices; and by Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the breath of the fasting mouth is more pleasant with Allah than the scent of musk."
"7175","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salamah from Hisham from Ibn Sirin who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying with hands on the waist."
"7176","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Salamah from Hisham from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands praying at night, let him begin with two light rakahs."
"7177","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Mamar, akhbarana Ibn Shihab from Ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell in clarified butter and died. He said: If it was solid, take it and what is around it, then eat what remains; and if it was liquid, do not eat it."
"7178","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, akhbarana Mamar, akhbarani Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Damdam from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing the two black ones in prayer. So I said to Yahya: What does he mean by the two black ones. He said: The snake and the scorpion."
"7179","Haddathana Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala from Mamar from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with his right; and when he removes, let him begin with his left. And he said: Wear them both together."
"7180","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Yunus from al-Hasan from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend enjoined upon me three: fasting three days of every month, and Witr before sleep, and ghusl on Friday."
"7181","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah; then his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian or make him a Magian, as the beast produces a beast; do you sense in it any mutilated."
"7182","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No child is born but Satan pricks him, so he begins crying screaming from the prick of Satan, except Ibn Maryam and his mother. Then Abu Hurayrah said: Recite if you wish: I seek refuge for her with You and her offspring from Satan the accursed."
"7183","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"7184","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Kisra perishes there is no Kisra after him, and when Qaysar perishes there is no Qaysar after him; and by Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, their treasures shall be spent in the path of Allah."
"7185","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer in congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five; and the angels of night and the angels of day gather in Fajr prayer. Then Abu Hurayrah says: Recite if you wish: And the recitation of dawn; the recitation of dawn is witnessed."
"7186","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Time draws near, and miserliness is cast, and trials appear, and harj increases. He said: They said: Which, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Killing, killing."
"7187","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab and from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman that they narrated to him from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam says: Not of those who earned anger nor of the astray, say Amin; for the angels say Amin, and the imam says Amin; so whoever his saying Amin coincides with the saying Amin of the angels shall be forgiven what preceded of his sin."
"7188","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits till it is finished has two qirats. They said: And what are the two qirats. He said: Like two great mountains."
"7189","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that a man of Banu Fazarah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, my wife bore a black boy, as if implying to disown him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you camels. He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors. He said: Red. He said: Among them a gray herd. He said: Yes, among them a gray herd. He said: And whence is that. He said: Perhaps a strain drew it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And this, perhaps a strain drew it."
"7190","Haddathana Yazid, akhbarana Ibn Abi Dhib from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that a Bedouin of Banu Fazarah shouted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife bore a black boy; and he mentioned its meaning."
"7191","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: to the Sacred Mosque, and this mosque of mine, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"7192","Haddathana Abd al-Ala, haddathana Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is the likeness of the crop; the wind keeps bending it, and the believer keeps affliction striking him; and the likeness of the hypocrite is as the cedar tree, not shaking till it is harvested."
"7193","Haddathana Abd al-Ala from Mamar from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They shall leave Madinah upon the best it was upon; none shall visit it but the seekers; he said meaning the seekers of beasts and birds; and the last to be gathered are two shepherds of Muzaynah calling to their sheep, and they find it wild, till when they reach Thaniyyat al-Wada they are gathered upon their faces, or fall upon their faces. He said: Whomever Allah wants good for He gives him understanding in religion; and I am only a distributor, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives."
"7194","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qirdusi and Yazid ibn Harun who said: Akhbarana Hisham from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The good deed is ten its likes, and fasting is Mine and I reward for it; he leaves his food and drink for Me; Yazid said: For My sake. Fasting is Mine and I reward for it; and the breath of the fasting mouth with Allah is more pleasant than the scent of musk."
"7195","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar, haddathana Hisham from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, a good deed is written for him; and if he does it, it is written for him ten its likes to seven hundred and seven its likes; and if he does not do it, a good deed is written for him; and whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, it is not written against him; and if he does it, one evil deed is written against him; and if he does not do it, it is not written against him."
"7196","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, haddathana Khalid from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A nation of Banu Israil was lost, not known what it did; and I see it only as the mouse; do you not see it, when camel milk is placed for it it does not drink, and when sheep milk is placed for it it drinks it. Abu Hurayrah said: I narrated this hadith to Kab, so he said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said: Yes. So he said that to me repeatedly. So I said: Do you read the Torah."
"7197","Haddathana Amr ibn al-Haytham ibn Qatan, and he is Abu Qatan, haddathana Hisham from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah who said: Abu Qatan said in the book, raised: When he sits between her four branches then exerts her, ghusl has become obligatory."
"7198","Haddathana Amr ibn al-Haytham, haddathana Ibn Abi Dhib from Ajlan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I look, or I surely look, at what is behind me as I look at what is before me; so straighten your rows and perfect your bowing and prostration."
"7199","Haddathana Amr ibn al-Haytham, haddathana Hisham from Yahya from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede Ramadan by a day nor two days, except a man who was fasting a fast, so let him fast it."
"7200","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Ibn Awn from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two afternoon prayers; Abu Hurayrah mentioned it and Muhammad forgot it; so he prayed two rakahs then greeted, and came to a timber laid across the mosque and put his hand upon it as if angry, and the hasty went out of the doors of the mosque saying: Prayer has been shortened. He said: And among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, but they feared to speak to him; and among the people was a man with length in his hands called Dhu al-Yadayn. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, have you forgotten or has prayer been shortened. So he said: I have not forgotten nor has prayer been shortened. He said: As Dhu al-Yadayn says. They said: Yes. So he came and prayed what he left, then greeted, then said takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised his head and said takbir. He said: So Muhammad would be asked: Then he greeted. So he says: I was told Imran ibn Husayn said: Then he greeted."
"7201","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Ibn Awn from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you, they are the most tender of hearts; faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni and understanding is Yemeni."
"7202","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Ibn Awn from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: None of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Not even I, unless my Lord envelops me with forgiveness and mercy, and not even I unless my Lord envelops me from Him with forgiveness and mercy, two times or three times."
"7203","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from al-Ala, and Muhammad ibn Jafar said: Haddathana Shubah who said: I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rights will surely be rendered to their owners on the Day of Resurrection, until retaliation is taken for the hornless sheep against the horned sheep that butted it. And Ibn Jafar said, meaning in his hadith: retribution is taken for the hornless sheep."
"7204","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from al-Ala, and Muhammad ibn Jafar: Haddathana Shubah who said: I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two who revile each other, whatever they say is upon the one who began, so long as the wronged one does not transgress."
"7205","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. My father said, and Muhammad ibn Jafar: Haddathana Shubah who said: I heard al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Charity does not decrease wealth, and no man pardons an injustice except that Allah increases him in honor, and no one humbled himself [source text breaks off here]."
"7206","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from al-Ala, and Ibn Jafar: Haddathana Shubah who said: I heard al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The false oath promotes the commodity and wipes out the earning. And Ibn Jafar said: the blessing."
"7207","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vows and said: It does not bring anything forward, but it extracts from the miser. And Ibn Jafar said: it is extracted thereby from the miser."
"7208","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah raises ranks and expiates sins: perfecting ablution in disliked circumstances, and many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer."
"7209","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer feels jealousy, the believer feels jealousy, the believer feels jealousy, and Allah is more jealous."
"7210","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Humayd from Bakr from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah who said: I met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was junub, so I walked with him until he sat, then I slipped away and came to the lodging and bathed, then I came while he was sitting. He said: Where were you. I said: You met me while I was junub, so I disliked sitting with you while I was junub, so I went and bathed. He said: Glory be to Allah, the believer does not become impure."
"7211","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of you. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best of you are the longest of you in age and the best of you in deeds. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I asked my father about al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father, and Suhayl from his father, and he said: I did not hear anyone mention al-Ala except with good, and he preferred Abu Salih over al-Ala."
"7212","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, from Barakah from Bashir ibn Nahik from Abu Hurayrah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stretching his hands until I could see the whiteness of his armpits. And Sulayman said, meaning in seeking rain."
"7213","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from Qatadah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adam from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah prescribed Friday upon those before us, so they differed about it, and Allah guided us to it; so people are our followers in it: tomorrow for the Jews and the day after tomorrow for the Christians."
"7214","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Haddathani Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Isa ibn Talhah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may utter a word seeing no harm in it, by which he falls seventy autumns into the Fire."
"7215","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Shubah from Qatadah from Khilas from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you catch a rakah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, then pray another upon it."
"7216","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Malik from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that two women of Banu Hudhayl, one of them threw at the other, so she miscarried a fetus; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged therein a ghurrah, a slave or a slave girl."
"7217","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah who said: If I saw gazelles in Madinah I would not frighten them; indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between its two lava tracts is sanctuary."
"7218","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman: Haddathana Malik from al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The strong is not the wrestler, but the strong is he who controls himself at anger."
"7219","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman: Haddathana Malik from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah that Abu Hurayrah used to say takbir whenever he lowered and raised, and would say: I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7220","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman: Haddathana Malik from al-Zuhri from Abu Idris from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution let him blow his nose, and whoever cleans with stones let him make it odd."
"7221","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Said ibn Abi Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a day and a night except with a mahram relative of her family."
"7222","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman: Haddathana Malik from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman from Hafs ibn Asim from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon my Basin."
"7223","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim from Ubaydah ibn Sufyan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every predator with fangs, eating it is unlawful."
"7224","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Travel is a portion of torment, preventing one of you his food and his drink and his sleep; so when one of you finishes his need of his travel, let him hasten to his family."
"7225","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in the call and the first row, then found nothing but to draw lots for it they would draw lots for it, and if they knew what is in early going they would race to it, and if they knew what is in Isha and Fajr they would come to them even crawling."
"7226","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Hour will not come until a man passes by the grave of a man and says: Would that I were in his place."
"7227","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Malik from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Hour will not come until impostor liars are sent, near thirty, each of them claiming that he is the Messenger of Allah."
"7228","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wisal, thus is my knowledge. They said: You practice wisal. He said: I am not like any of you; I spend the night fed by my Lord and given drink."
"7229","Haddathana Ibn Mahdi from Malik from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not come to prayer while you are running, and come to it with tranquility upon you; so what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"7230","Haddathana Ibn Mahdi from Malik from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not come to prayer while you are running, and come to it with tranquility upon you; so what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"7231","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman: Haddathana Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to a town consuming towns; they say Yathrib, and it is Madinah; it expels people as the bellows expels the dross of iron."
"7232","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Safwan ibn Sulaym from Said ibn Salamah of the family of Ibn al-Azraq from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Burdah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said about the water of the sea: It is pure, its water; lawful, its dead."
"7233","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Nuaym ibn Abd Allah that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the passes of Madinah are angels; neither the Dajjal nor the plague enters it."
"7234","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Sasah from Said ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whomever Allah intends good for, He afflicts him."
"7235","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Malik from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from Abu Sufyan from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted araya to be sold by its estimate in five wasqs or less than five."
"7236","Haddathana al-Walid ibn Muslim Abu al-Abbas: Haddathana al-Awzai: Haddathani Hassan ibn Atiyyah: Haddathani Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finishes the last tashahhud, let him seek refuge from four: from the torment of Hell, and from the torment of the grave, and from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the Masih al-Dajjal."
"7237","Haddathana al-Walid: Haddathana al-Awzai: Haddathani al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: Prayer was established and people arranged their rows, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and stood at his place, then gestured to them with his hand: Stay in your place. Then he went out having bathed, his head dripping, and prayed with them."
"7238","Haddathana al-Walid: Haddathana al-Awzai: Haddathani al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet nor ruler except he has two confidants: a confidant commanding him to good, and a confidant not sparing him corruption; and whoever is protected from their evil is protected, and he is with the one that prevails over him of them."
"7239","Haddathana al-Walid: Haddathana al-Awzai: Haddathana al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, on the morrow of the Day of Sacrifice while at Mina: Tomorrow we will alight at the Khayf of Banu Kinanah where they divided upon disbelief, meaning thereby al-Muhassab; and that is that Quraysh and Kinanah allied against Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib that they would not intermarry them nor trade with them until they surrender to them the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7240","Haddathana al-Walid: Haddathana al-Awzai: Haddathani Qurrah from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah Almighty says: The most beloved of My servants to Me are the quickest of them in breaking fast."
"7241","Haddathana al-Walid: Haddathana al-Awzai: Haddathana Yahya from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah. My father said, and Abu Dawud said: Haddathana Harb from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir who said: Haddathani Abu Salamah: Haddathana Abu Hurayrah, the meaning, who said: When Allah granted His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among them and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Allah withheld the Elephant from Makkah and gave His Messenger and the believers power over it; it was made lawful for me only for an hour of the day, then it is sanctuary until the Day of Resurrection: its trees are not cut, its game is not frightened, and its lost property is not lawful except for one who announces it. And whoever is killed having one killed, he has the better of two views: either he takes blood money or he kills. Then a man of the people of Yemen called Abu Shah stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, write for me. He said: Write for him. The uncle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except idhkhir, for it is for our graves and our houses. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except idhkhir. I said to al-Awzai: What is his saying, write for Abu Shah, and what is it they write for him. He said: He says: Write for him his sermon that he heard. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Nothing is narrated about the writing of hadith more authentic than this hadith, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them, he said: Write for Abu Shah what he heard of the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7242","Haddathana al-Walid: Haddathana al-Awzai: Haddathani Hassan ibn Atiyyah: Haddathani Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah from Abu Hurayrah that he narrated to them that Abu Dharr said: O Messenger of Allah, the owners of wealth have gone with the rewards: they pray as we pray and fast as we fast, and they have surplus wealth with which they give charity, and we have nothing with which to give charity. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to words which if you act by them you catch those who preceded you, and none catches you except one who acts like your deed. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You say takbir after every prayer thirty-three times, and tasbih thirty-three times, and tahmid thirty-three times, and seal it with: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner has He; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable."
"7243","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyaynah who said: We memorized it from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If the reciter says amin, then say amin, for the angels say amin; so whoever his amin coincides with the amin of the angels, forgiven him what preceded of his sin."
"7244","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: The son of Adam hurts Me; he reviles time, and I am time; in My hand is the command, I turn night and day."
"7245","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When heat intensifies, cool with prayer, for intense heat is from the blast of Hell."
"7246","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Fire complained to its Lord and said: Part of me ate part of me; so He permitted it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer; so the severest heat is from the blast of Hell."
"7247","Haddathana Sufyan: Haddathana al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a townsman selling for a Bedouin, or bidding up against one another, or a man proposing over the proposal of his brother, or selling over the sale of his brother; and a woman must not ask the divorce of her sister to empty what is in her bowl or her vessel; let her marry, for her provision is upon Allah."
"7248","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Journeys are tied to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and my mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque. Sufyan said: And journeys are not tied except to three mosques alike."
"7249","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah; it was said to him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes: If you come to prayer, do not come to it while you are running, and come to it with tranquility upon you; so what you catch, pray, and what you miss, make up."
"7250","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in one garment. He said: Do all of you have two garments. Abu Hurayrah said: Do you know Abu Hurayrah praying in one garment while his clothes are on the rack."
"7251","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq: Akhbarana Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak: Akhbarana Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not come to prayer while you are running, but walk to it with tranquility upon you; so what you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"7252","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."
"7253","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said and Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The untended animal, its wound is void, and the mine is void, and the well is void, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"7254","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah: A Bedouin entered the mosque and prayed two rakahs, then said: O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not have mercy with us on anyone. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him and said: You have narrowed something wide. Then he did not remain but that he urinated in the mosque, so people hastened to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: You were sent as facilitators and were not sent as complicators; pour upon it a bucket of water or a basin of water."
"7255","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No fara and no atirah."
"7256","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and it was said to him once: You raised it, and he said: Yes; and he said once, conveying it: They say al-karm, rather al-karm is the heart of the believer."
"7257","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If it is Friday, upon every door of the doors of the mosque are angels writing the first then the first; so when the imam comes out, the scrolls are folded."
"7258","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The early comer to Friday is like one offering a camel, then the one next him like one offering a cow, and the one next him like one offering a ram, until he mentioned the chicken and the egg."
"7259","Haddathana Sufyan: Haddathana al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from the last rakah of the Fajr prayer, he said: O Allah, save al-Walid ibn al-Walid and Salamah ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah and the weak in Makkah; O Allah, tighten Your grip upon Mudar and make it upon them years like the years of Yusuf."
"7260","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Sufyan said once, as a narration: Five are of fitrah: circumcision, and shaving, and trimming the mustache, and clipping the nails, and plucking the armpit."
"7261","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah, or from Abu Salamah, from one of them or both, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"7262","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Hour will not come until you fight a people as if their faces are hammered shields, their sandals hair."
"7263","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah: A man of Banu Fazarah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife bore a black boy. He said: Have you camels. He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors. He said: Red. He said: Is there among them grey. He said: Among them are grey. He said: How did that come to it. He said: Perhaps a strain drew it. He said: And this, perhaps a strain drew it."
"7264","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No Muslim loses three children then enters the Fire except to fulfill the oath."
"7265","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The earth was made for me a mosque and a purification. Sufyan said: I think it from Said from Abu Hurayrah. Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah, as a narration: Hasten with your funerals, for if he was righteous you bring him forward to it, and if he was other than that, it is evil you put off your necks. And he said another time, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Hasten with the funeral, for if it is righteous, good you bring it forward to it."
"7266","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If Khosrau perishes there is no Khosrau after him, and if Caesar perishes there is no Caesar after him; and by Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, their treasures will surely be spent in the way of Allah."
"7267","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He is about to descend among you, Ibn Maryam, as a just judge: he breaks the cross and kills the pig and abolishes the jizyah, and wealth overflows until none accepts it."
"7268","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri: He heard Ibn Ukaymah narrating to Said ibn al-Musayyab, saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer thought to be Fajr; when he finished his prayer he said: Did any of you recite. A man said: I. He said: I say, why is the Quran contested with me. Mamar said from al-Zuhri: So people stopped reciting in what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites aloud. Sufyan said: This word was hidden from me."
"7269","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq: Haddathana Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak: Akhbarana Yunus from al-Zuhri: Haddathana Abu Umamah ibn Sahl that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hasten with the funeral, for if it was righteous you bring it near to good, and if it was other than that, evil you put off your necks. My father said: Sufyan agreed with Mamar and Ibn Abi Hafsah."
"7270","Haddathana Ali ibn Ishaq from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ibn Abi Hafsah [no matn in source; isnad only]."
"7271","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Hanzalah al-Aslami: He heard Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, Ibn Maryam will surely raise his voice with talbiyah at Fajj al-Rawha as a pilgrim or an umrah performer, or will join both."
"7272","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar: They heard Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Jews and the Christians do not dye, so differ from them."
"7273","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: You claim that Abu Hurayrah narrates much upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah is the appointor. I was a poor man staying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the fill of my belly, and the Muhajirun were busy trading in the markets, and the Ansar were busy attending their properties; so I attended a sitting of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Who spreads his cloak until I finish my saying, then draws it to him, will never forget anything he heard from me. And I spread a cloak upon me until he finished his hadith, then I drew it to me; so by Him in Whose hand is my soul, I did not forget anything after I heard it from him."
"7274","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa: Akhbarana Malik from al-Zuhri from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah that he said: People say Abu Hurayrah narrated much; by Allah, were it not for two verses in the Book of Allah I would not narrate a hadith. Then he recites these two verses: Those who conceal what We sent down of clear proofs and guidance, then he mentioned the hadith."
"7275","Haddathana Abu al-Yaman: Akhbarana Shuayb from al-Zuhri: Akhbarana Said ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman that Abu Hurayrah said: You say Abu Hurayrah narrates much, then he mentioned it."
"7276","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, and it was read to him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If one of you asks his neighbor to fix timber in his wall, let him not prevent him. When Abu Hurayrah narrated them they lowered their heads, so he said: Why do I see you turning away. By Allah, I will surely throw it between your shoulders."
"7277","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah. Sufyan said: I asked him about it, how is the food, meaning the food of the rich. He said: al-Araj informed me from Abu Hurayrah: The worst food is the wedding feast to which the rich are invited and the poor are left; and whoever does not come to the invitation disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"7278","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and reckoning, forgiven him what preceded of his sin. My father said: I heard it four times from Sufyan, and he said once: Whoever fasts Ramadan, and he said once: Whoever stands, and: Whoever stands Laylat al-Qadr with faith and reckoning, forgiven him what preceded of his sin."
"7279","Haddathana Ismail ibn Umar: Akhbarana Ibn Abi Dhib from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) encouraging standing, meaning Ramadan."
"7280","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, as a narration: If one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand in his vessel until he washes it thrice, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"7281","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the Negus died, informed them that he died; seek forgiveness for him."
"7282","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever catches a rakah of prayer has caught it."
"7283","Haddathana Sufyan who said: I heard al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Tasbih is for men and clapping is for women."
"7284","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and confuses him until he does not know how much he prayed; so whoever finds anything of that, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"7285","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah, if Allah wills, from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Upon you is this black seed, for in it is healing from every disease except sam. Sufyan said: Sam is death, and it is shuniz."
"7286","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah or Said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat to be used for nabidh. And Abu Hurayrah says: Avoid hantam."
"7287","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah: Al-Aqra saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing Hasan, so he said: I have ten children, I never kissed any of them. He said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"7288","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah that he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am ruined. He said: What ruined you. He said: I fell upon my wife in Ramadan. He said: Do you find a slave. He said: No. He said: Can you fast two consecutive months. He said: No. He said: Can you feed sixty poor. He said: No. He said: Sit. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket with dates in it, and the basket is the huge pannier. He said: Give charity with this. He said: Upon poorer than us; between its two lava tracts there is none poorer than us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: Feed it to your family. And he said once: So he smiled until his molars appeared, and said: Feed it to your dependents."
"7289","Haddathana Sufyan: Akhbarani al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub al-Huraqi in his house upon his bed, from his father from Abu Hurayrah: Any prayer in which the Fatihat al-Kitab is not recited is deficient, then it is deficient, then it is deficient. He said: Abu Hurayrah said, and he said before that: My beloved, upon him prayer and peace, said. He said: So he said: O Persian, recite the Fatihat al-Kitab, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah Almighty said: I divided prayer between Me and My servant, and he said once: For My servant is what he asked. So when he says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of worlds, He says: My servant praised Me. So when he says: The Merciful, the Compassionate, He says: My servant glorified Me, or: My servant extolled Me. So when he says: Master of the Day of Judgment, He says: My servant entrusted to Me. So when he says: You we worship and You we ask help, He says: This is between Me and My servant, and for My servant is what he asked. And he said once: What he asked Me. Then His servant asks Him: Guide us the straight path, the path of those You favored upon them, not of those angered upon nor the strayers. He says: This is for My servant, for you what you asked. And he said once: And for My servant what he asked Me."
"7290","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man selling food and asked him: How do you sell. So he told him, then it was revealed to him: Put your hand in it. So he put his hand in, and it was wet. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who cheats is not of us."
"7291","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The false oath promotes the commodity and wipes out the earning."
"7292","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Ala from his father from Abu Hurayrah, raising it: If one of you yawns, let him place his hand upon his mouth."
"7293","Haddathana Sufyan from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Irak from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no charity upon the Muslim for his horse nor his slave."
"7294","Haddathana Sufyan: Haddathana Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah Almighty said: If My servant intends a good deed, write it; so if he does it, write it ten likes it. And if he intends an evil deed, do not write it; so if he does it, write it like it. So if he leaves it, write it a good deed."
"7295","Haddathana Sufyan from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah Almighty said: The vow does not bring the son of Adam anything I did not decree for him, but it is a thing I extract thereby from the miser; he gives Me thereby what he does not give Me upon miserliness."
"7296","Haddathana Sufyan from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah Almighty says: O son of Adam, spend, I spend upon you. And he said: The right hand of Allah is full, flowing, nothing diminishes it night and day."
"7297","Haddathana Sufyan from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, as a narration, who said: Allah Almighty said: My mercy preceded My anger."
"7298","Haddathana Sufyan: Haddathana Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you performs ablution, let him put in his nose then let him blow out. And he said once: Let him blow."
"7299","Haddathana Sufyan from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there not a man who grants a household a she-camel going in the morning with a bowl and returning in the evening with a bowl; its reward is great."
"7300","Haddathana Sufyan from Abu al-Zinad and Ibn Ajlan from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one is wounded in the way of Allah, and Allah knows who is wounded in His way, except he comes on the Day of Resurrection with the wound bleeding blood: the color color of blood, and the smell smell of musk. And Sufyan singled it once from Abu al-Zinad."
"7301","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it, and once he said, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My heirs do not divide up a dinar or a dirham; whatever I leave after the maintenance of my wives and the provision of my servant is charity."
"7302","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you is invited to food while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting. My father said: We did not give him the kunya Abu al-Zinad; we used to give him the kunya Abu Abd al-Rahman."
"7303","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet traders on the way, and do not withhold milk in sheep and camels for sale; whoever buys such an animal after that has the choice of the two views: if he wishes he keeps it, and if he wishes he returns it with a sa of dates, not samra."
"7304","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People follow Quraysh in this matter; their Muslims follow their Muslims and their disbelievers follow their disbelievers."
"7305","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man does not pray in a single garment with nothing of it on his shoulders; and once he said: his shoulder."
"7306","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Satan ties three knots on the back of the head of one of you, striking upon each knot: A long night is upon you, so sleep; and once he said: striking upon him with each knot: a long night; he said: When he wakes and remembers Allah, Mighty and Majestic, one knot is undone; when he performs ablution, two knots are undone; when he prays, the knots are undone, and he rises in the morning cheerful and energetic; otherwise he rises in the morning evil-spirited and lazy."
"7307","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah: A swarm of locusts of gold was rained down upon Ayyub, and he began gathering them into his garment; it was said: O Ayyub, was what I gave you not enough for you; he said: O Lord, who can do without Your bounty."
"7308","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last and we are the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that every nation, and once he said: except that, and Ibn Tawus combined it and said: One of them said: except that, and the other said: apart from, every nation was given the Book before us and we were given it after them; then this is the day which Allah prescribed for them and they differed over it, so Allah guided us to it; people follow us in it: the Jews have tomorrow and the Christians the day after tomorrow."
"7309","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am only a human; I become angry as humans become angry; so whichever man I have harmed or flogged, make it for him purification and prayer."
"7310","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A town-dweller does not sell for a bedouin."
"7311","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If a man peeps, and once he said: if a person peeps, without your permission and you throw a pebble at him and gouge his eye, there is no sin upon you."
"7312","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you supplicates, let him not say: O Allah, forgive me if You will; rather let him be resolute in asking, for none compels Him."
"7313","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Al-Tufayl ibn Amr al-Dawsi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Daws has disobeyed and refused, so supplicate against them; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the qibla and raised his hands, and the people said: They are doomed; then he said: O Allah, guide Daws and bring them; O Allah, guide Daws and bring them."
"7314","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Richness is not from abundance of goods; rather richness is richness of the soul."
"7315","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): By Allah, for one of you to take a rope and gather firewood and carry it on his back and eat from it or give charity is better for him than to come to a man whom Allah has enriched from His bounty and ask him, whether he gives him or withholds from him; that is because the upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"7316","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He does not steal while he steals and he is a believer, and he does not drink wine while he drinks it and he is a believer, and he does not commit adultery while he commits adultery and he is a believer."
"7317","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): None of you should look at whoever is above him in creation or character or wealth; rather he should look at whoever is below him."
"7318","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The food of two suffices three, and the food of three suffices four; my likeness and the likeness of people is like a man who kindles a fire, and when it lights up what is around him, moths and crawling creatures begin plunging into it; so I am holding you by your waist-wrappers while you are falling into it; and with its isnad: The likeness of the prophets is like a man who built a building and made it good and perfect and beautiful, and people began circling it saying: We have never seen a building more beautiful than this except for this breach; so I am that breach; and it was said to Sufyan: Who mentioned this; he said: Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah."
"7319","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face, for Allah created Adam in His image."
"7320","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Surplus water is not withheld so that herbage may thereby be withheld; Sufyan said: There is herbage around your well, so you withhold your surplus water from them, and they cannot but leave off."
"7321","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"7322","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah, Mighty and Majestic, indeed laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other and both enter Paradise together; he says: He was a disbeliever who killed a Muslim, then the disbeliever embraced Islam before he died, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, admitted them both into Paradise."
"7323","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Amr from Yahya ibn Jadah: This fire of yours is a part of seventy parts of the Fire of Hell, and it was struck with the sea twice; were it not for that, Allah would not have made any benefit in it for anyone."
"7324","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I indeed intended to order a man to lead the prayer, then order my youths, and Sufyan once said: youths, to go instead to people who do not attend it and burn their houses over them with bundles of firewood; and if one of you knew he would find a fat bone or two good trotters, he would attend the prayers; and Sufyan once said: al-Isha."
"7325","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The most abject name before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a man named king of kings; I asked Abu Amr al-Shaybani about the most abject name before Allah, and he said: The lowest name before Allah."
"7326","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of continuous fasting; they said: O Messenger of Allah, you practice continuous fasting; he said: I am not like any one of you; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"7327","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not wonder how Allah diverts from me the abuse of Quraysh; how they curse Mudhammam and revile Mudhammam, while I am Muhammad."
"7328","He said: It was read out to Sufyan: I heard Abu al-Zinad narrating from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When you say to your companion on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon: Be quiet, you have engaged in idle talk; Sufyan said: Abu al-Zinad said: It is the dialect of Abu Hurayrah."
"7329","He said: It was read out to Sufyan: Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I indeed see your humility."
"7330","He said: It was read out to Sufyan: I heard Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I heard Sufyan say: Whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"7331","My father said, and Sufyan said in the hadith of Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn Jurayj from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Tawus from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The coat of mail extended, or passed, covering his fingertips and effacing his trace; he widens it; Abu al-Zinad said: He widens it and it does not widen; Ibn Jurayj said: from al-Hasan ibn Muslim: And it does not expand."
"7332","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah; it was said to Sufyan: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Yes: The delay of the rich is injustice, and when one of you is referred to a solvent man, let him follow up."
"7333","He said: It was read out to Sufyan: I heard Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I heard Sufyan say: Beware of suspicion, for it is the falsest speech."
"7334","I heard Sufyan say: When the servant suffices one of you his food, let him seat him to eat with him; if he does not do so, let him take a morsel and dip it in it and hand it to him; and its isnad was read out to him: I heard Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7335","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my nation, I would have commanded them with the tooth-stick at every prayer and with delaying al-Isha."
"7336","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, as a narration, he said, once tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you wakes fasting, let him not utter obscenity or act ignorantly; and if a man reviles him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting."
"7337","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You find among the worst of people the two-faced one who comes to these with a face and to these with a face."
"7338","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my nation, I would have commanded them with delaying al-Isha and the tooth-stick with the prayer; and no woman fasts while her husband is present a day other than Ramadan except with his permission; and this hadith was read out to him: I heard Abu al-Zinad from Musa ibn Abi Uthman from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7339","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my nation, the believers, I would not have stayed behind from an expedition; I have nothing with me to mount them upon, and they would not stay behind from me."
"7340","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, raising it: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times, for Allah is Odd and loves the odd."
"7341","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Perhaps it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven washings."
"7342","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah: The best charity is what is given from surplus wealth, and begin with those you maintain."
"7343","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and let him take off the left; and when the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal; let him take them both off together or wear them both together."
"7344","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from Musa ibn Abi Uthman from his father, or from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it; he said: It is a sacrificial camel; he said: Ride it; he said: It is a sacrificial camel; he said: Ride it; and he had no doubt about it; once he said: From Musa ibn Abi Uthman from his father from Abu Hurayrah."
"7345","Sufyan narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer, then turned to us with his face and said: While a man was driving a cow, he rode it and struck it; it said: We were not created for this; we were created for ploughing; the people said: Glory be to Allah, a cow speaks; then he said: I believe in this, I and Abu Bakr, tomorrow, tomorrow, and Umar, though the two were not there; and while a man was among his sheep, a wolf pounced upon them and took a sheep from them; he pursued it and caught up with it and rescued it from him; it said: O man, you rescued it from me, so who will care for it on the day of the predator, the day when it has no shepherd other than me; the people said: Glory be to Allah, a wolf speaks; then he said: I believe in that, and Abu Bakr and Umar, though the two were not there."
"7346","Sufyan narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Sad from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah from Abu Maymunah from Abu Hurayrah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a man and a woman and their son a choice, and he gave the boy a choice; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O boy, this is your father and this is your mother; choose."
"7347","Sufyan narrated to us: I asked him about Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever follows it until its matter is finished has two qirats, the smaller of the two, or one of the two, like Uhud."
"7348","Sufyan narrated to us: Sumayy narrated to me from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and the two Umrahs, or Umrah to Umrah, expiates what is between them."
"7349","Sufyan narrated to us from Sumayy from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from these three: reaching misery, the gloating of enemies, and the evil of the decree, or the hardship of the decree; Sufyan said: I added one myself; I do not know which of them it is."
"7350","Sufyan narrated to us from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab from the freedman of Ibn Abi Ruhm, who heard it from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Hurayrah met a perfumed woman and said: Where are you going, O slave-girl of the Almighty; she said: To the mosque; he said: And did you perfume yourself for it; she said: Yes; Abu Hurayrah said: He said: Any woman who leaves her house perfumed intending the mosque, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not accept a prayer from her until she returns and washes herself from it as she washes from janaba."
"7351","Sufyan narrated to us: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah: Some women came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot reach you in your assembly because of the men, so promise us a day from you when we may come to you; he said: Your appointment is the house of so-and-so; and he came to them on that day and for that appointment; he said: Among what he said to them, meaning: There is no woman who sends forth three children, anticipating reward, except that she enters Paradise; then a woman among them said: Or two; he said: Or two."
"7352","Sufyan narrated to us from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, do not make my grave an idol; Allah cursed people who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"7353","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn al-Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it, for in one of its wings is a cure and in the other is a disease."
"7354","Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, and it was read out to Sufyan, from Said from Abu Hurayrah, who used to say, then Sufyan said: It is like this, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When he lays his side down, he says: In Your name, my Lord, I lay my side; if You withhold my soul, have mercy upon it, and if You release it, guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants."
"7355","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, and it was read out to Sufyan, from Said from Abu Hurayrah, if Allah wills; Sufyan said: What we heard from him from Ibn Ajlan, I do not know from whom; Sufyan was asked about Thumamah ibn Uthal, and he said: The Muslims had captured him, they seized him, and whenever he passed by him he would say: What do you have, O Thumamah; he would say: If you kill, you kill one with blood, and if you bestow favor, you bestow it upon a grateful one, and if you want wealth, you are given wealth; he said: Whenever he passed by him he would say: What do you have, O Thumamah; he would say: If you bestow favor, you bestow it upon a grateful one, and if you kill, you kill one with blood, and if you want wealth, you are given wealth; he said: It then occurred to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to release him, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, cast into his heart; he said: They took him to the well of the Ansar and washed him, and he embraced Islam and said: O Muhammad, yesterday your face was the most hateful of faces to me, and your religion the most hateful of religions to me, and your town the most hateful of towns to me; now your religion is the most beloved of religions to me, and your face the most beloved of faces to me; no grain shall come to Quraysh from al-Yamamah, until Umar said: By Allah, he was in my eyes smaller than a pig, and now he is in my eyes greater than a mountain; he released him, and he went to al-Yamamah and withheld from them, so they clamored and complained, and they wrote: Order kinship; he said: And he wrote to him; and I heard him say: from Sufyan: I heard Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah that Thumamah ibn Uthal said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7356","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah, as a narration: The best rows of men are the first of them and the worst of them are the last of them, and the best rows of women are the last of them and the worst rows of women are the first of them."
"7357","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah al-Dawsi, he said: Then he gifted him a she-camel, meaning his saying, he said: I accept a gift only from a Qurashi or a Dawsi or a Thaqafi."
"7358","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah from Ajlan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The slave has his food and his clothing, and you do not burden him with work he cannot bear."
"7359","Harun narrated to us from Ibn Wahb: Amr narrated to us that Bukayr narrated to him from al-Ajlan the freedman of Fatimah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The slave has his food and his clothing, and he is not burdened with work he cannot bear."
"7360","He said: It was read out to Sufyan: I heard Ibn Ajlan from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah from Ajlan from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We have not made peace with them since we fought them, meaning snakes."
"7361","Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you; those before you perished only through their excessive questioning and their differing over their prophets; what I forbid you, refrain from, and what I command you, do from it what you can."
"7362","Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am to you only like a father; when you go to the privy, do not face the qibla nor turn your backs to it; and he forbade dung and decayed bones; and a man does not clean himself with his right hand."
"7363","He said: It was read out to Sufyan: from Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May Allah have mercy upon a man who rises at night; Sufyan said: Do not sprinkle on his face, you wipe it."
"7364","Sufyan narrated to us from Yahya from Said ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I was commanded to a town that consumes towns; they say Yathrib, but it is al-Madina; it expels people as the bellows expels the dross of iron."
"7365","Sufyan narrated to us from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Bakr al-Ansari from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Bakr al-Makhzumi from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in When the sky is rent asunder and Read."
"7366","Sufyan narrated to us from Yahya from Abu Bakr from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever finds his property with a bankrupt man has the most right to it."
"7367","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Ikrimah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I narrate to you brief things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A man does not drink from the mouth of the waterskin."
"7368","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He prostrated them after the salutation."
"7369","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub from Muhammad: Men and women disputed which of them are more in Paradise, then Abu Hurayrah said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to enter Paradise are like the moon on the night of the full moon, then those who follow them like the brightest piercing star; for each man among them are two wives, the marrow of whose shins is seen from behind the flesh; and there is no unmarried person in Paradise."
"7370","Sufyan narrated to us: He heard Ayyub from Muhammad ibn Sirin saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: He prayed, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), one of the two afternoon prayers, either al-Zuhr, and most of my thought is that it was al-Asr, and he gave salutation after two; then he went to a trunk which he used to pray toward and sat by it angrily; and Sufyan said: Then he went to a trunk in the qibla against which he used to lean his back, and he leaned his back against it; he said: Then the hasty people went out and said: The prayer has been shortened; and among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar; he said: It has not been shortened, and I have not forgotten; he said: You prayed only two; he said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked, and they said: Yes; then he stood and prayed two, then gave salutation, then said takbir and prostrated like his prostration or longer, then raised and said takbir, then prostrated and said takbir."
"7371","He said: It was read out to Sufyan: I heard Ayyub from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Name yourselves by my name and do not take my kunya."
"7372","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Name yourselves by my name and do not take my kunya."
"7373","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I memorized from Mamar from Yahya, he informed him, from Damdam from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of the two black things in prayer: the scorpion and the snake."
"7374","Sufyan narrated to us from Mamar from Ayyub from Ibn Sirin; it was said to Sufyan: From Abu Hurayrah; he said: Yes; it was said to him: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Yes: Whoever buys an animal with withheld milk, whether muhaffalah or musarrah, has the choice; if he wishes to return it, let him return it, and if he wishes to keep it, let him keep it."
"7375","Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever comes to this House without uttering obscenity or committing sin returns as on the day his mother bore him."
"7376","Sufyan narrated to us from Ata ibn al-Saib from al-Agharr from Abu Hurayrah; Sufyan said: The first time: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he repeated it and said: al-Agharr from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Pride is My cloak and might is My garment; whoever contends with Me for one of them, I cast him into the Fire."
"7377","Sufyan narrated to us from Zaidah from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The truest verse the poet said is: Is it not that everything besides Allah is vain; and Ibn Abi al-Salt almost embraced Islam."
"7378","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Abu al-Awbar from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray standing and sitting, barefoot and shod."
"7379","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, and he added in it: And he turns from his right and from his left."
"7380","Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Muhaysin, a Qurashi Sahmi shaykh, narrated to me, who heard it from Muhammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it was revealed, it weighed heavily upon the Muslims and reached among them what Allah willed it to reach; they complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Draw near and be right; everything that befalls the Muslim is expiation, even the stumble he stumbles."
"7381","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr: He heard Tawus; he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa, peace be upon them both, argued; Musa said: O Adam, you are our father; you disappointed us and expelled us from Paradise; Adam said to him: O Musa, Allah chose you with His speech, and once he said: with His message, and wrote for you with His hand; do you blame me for a matter which Allah decreed for me forty years before He created me; he said: Adam overcame Musa; Adam overcame Musa."
"7382","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Yahya ibn Jadah from Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Qari, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: No, by the Lord of this House, I did not say: Whoever wakes junub does not fast; Muhammad, by the Lord of the House, said it; I did not forbid fasting on Friday; Muhammad forbade it, by the Lord of the House."
"7383","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Ibn Munabbih, meaning Wahb, from his brother: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: There is none with more hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than I except Abd Allah ibn Amr, for he used to write and I did not write."
"7384","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Hisham ibn Yahya from Abu Hurayrah, and Yahya from Abu Bakr from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever finds his property with a bankrupt man has the most right to it."
"7385","Sufyan narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayyah: He heard it from a shaykh, then once he said: I heard it from a desert man, a bedouin: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reads By those sent forth in succession and reaches In what discourse after it will they believe, let him say: We believe in Allah; and whoever reads By the fig and the olive, let him say: Yes, and I am among the witnesses to that; and whoever reads Is He not able to give life to the dead, let him say: Yes; Ismail said: I went to see whether he had memorized, and he was a bedouin, and he said: O son of my brother, did you think I had not memorized it; I have performed sixty pilgrimages, and there is none of them in which I do not know the camel upon which I performed it."
"7386","Sufyan narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Abu Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hurayth al-Udhri, he said once: From Abu Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Hurayth, from his grandfather: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him place something before his face; if he finds nothing, let him set up a stick; if he has no stick with him, let him draw a line; and whatever passes before him will not harm him."
"7387","Sufyan narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Abu Amr ibn Hurayth from his father from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, then he mentioned its meaning."
"7388","And Abd al-Razzaq said: Mamar and al-Thawri informed us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Abu Amr ibn Hurayth from his father from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, then he mentioned the hadith."
"7389","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery and her adultery becomes evident, let him flog her the prescribed hadd and not reproach her; Sufyan said: Not reproach her means not taunt her; concerning it, on the third or the fourth, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."
"7390","Sufyan narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Musa informed us from Ata ibn Mina: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I prostrated with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in When the sky is rent asunder and Read in the name of your Lord."
"7391","Sufyan narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Musa from Makhul from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no charity upon the Muslim for his slave or his horse."
"7392","Sufyan narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me from Nafi ibn Jubayr from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to Hasan: O Allah, I love him, so love him and love whoever loves him."
"7393","Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Tawus from his father from Abu Hurayrah, and Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah, tracing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We are the last and we are the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that every nation was given the Book before us and we were given it after them; then this is the day which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, prescribed for them and they differed over it, so Allah guided us to it; people follow us in it: the Jews have tomorrow and the Christians the day after tomorrow; one of them said: except that, and the other said: apart from."
"7394","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Suhayl ibn Abi Salih mentioning from his father from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray after Friday, pray four; and if something hurries you, pray two in the mosque and two when you return; Ibn Idris said: I do not know whether this hadith belongs to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or not."
"7395","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them; and it is the day they were commanded with and they differed over it, so Allah made it a festival for us; today is ours, and tomorrow is for the Jews, and the day after tomorrow is for the Christians."
"7396","Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most perfect of the believers in faith are the best of them in character, and the best of them are the best of them to their wives."
"7397","Abdah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given concise speech, and the earth was made for me a mosque and purification."
"7398","Ismail narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman is consulted about herself, and the virgin is asked permission; they said: O Messenger of Allah, how is her permission; he said: That she remain silent."
"7399","Ismail narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Mihran narrated to me from Abu Rafi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spit in the qibla of the mosque and turned to the people and said: What is with one of you who stands facing his Lord and spits before him; would one of you like to be faced and spat in his face; when one of you spits, let him spit to his left or under his foot; and if he finds nothing, let him spit like this in his garment; then al-Qasim described: He spat in his garment then rubbed part of it with part."
"7400","Ismail narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub informed me that Abu al-Saib informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not read the Mother of the Book, it is defective, incomplete; I said: O Abu Hurayrah, I am sometimes behind the imam; then he squeezed my arm and said: O Persian, recite it to yourself."
"7401","Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us from Umarah ibn al-Qaqa from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked which charity is most excellent. He said: You shall surely be told: that you give charity while you are healthy and miserly, hoping to live and fearing poverty, and do not delay until when it reaches the throat you say: For so-and-so such-and-such and for so-and-so such-and-such, when it has already come to belong to so-and-so."
"7402","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Sufyan who said: Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Abu Zurah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike shikal in horses."
"7403","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, al-Qaqa ibn Hakim narrated to me from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am to you only like a father, I teach you. When one of you goes to the privy, do not face it nor turn your backs to it, and let him not clean himself with his right hand. And he used to command three stones and forbid dung and decayed bone."
"7404","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, al-Qaqa ibn Hakim narrated to me from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a man who stands in the night and prays and wakes his wife and she prays, and if she refuses he sprinkles water on her face. And may Allah have mercy on a woman who stands in the night and prays and wakes her husband and he prays, and if he refuses she sprinkles water on his face."
"7405","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ubayd Allah from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale by pebbles and the sale involving uncertainty."
"7406","Yahya narrated to us, Ubayd Allah informed us, Ibn Abi Said narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I not feared hardship for my community I would have commanded them to use the tooth-stick with ablution, and I would have delayed the night prayer to a third of the night or half the night."
"7407","Yahya narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Thabit al-Zuraqi narrated to me who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the wind, for it comes with mercy and punishment, but ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Him from its evil."
"7408","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib who said: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel for a day except with a male kin."
"7409","Yahya narrated to us from Yahya, Dhakwan Abu Salih narrated to me from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah or Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim, Yahya doubted, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."
"7410","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three, all of them have a right upon Allah to aid them: the warrior in the path of Allah, the one who marries seeking chastity, and the contracted slave seeking to pay."
"7411","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan who said: I heard my father from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My eye sleeps but my heart does not sleep."
"7412","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man said: How much suffices for my head in washing from major impurity? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour with his hand upon his head three times. He said: My hair is abundant. He said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more abundant and better."
"7413","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity. A man said: I have a dinar. He said: Give it in charity to yourself. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Give it in charity to your wife. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Give it in charity to your child. He said: I have another dinar. He said: Give it in charity to your servant. He said: I have another dinar. He said: You know best."
"7414","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you strikes, let him avoid the face, and do not say: May Allah disgrace your face and the face of whoever resembles your face, for Allah the Exalted created Adam upon his image."
"7415","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked which women are best. He said: The one who pleases him when he looks, obeys him when he commands, and does not oppose him in herself and his wealth in what he dislikes."
"7416","Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr both said: Shubah narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: I am with My servant when he remembers Me. If he remembers Me to himself I remember him to Myself, and if he remembers Me in a company I remember him in a company better than them. If he draws near to Me a span I draw near to him a cubit, and if he draws near to Me a cubit I draw near to him a fathom. If he comes to Me walking I come to him hastening. And Ibn Numayr said in his hadith: I am at the opinion of My servant of Me and I am with him wherever he remembers Me."
"7417","Abu Muawiyah and Yala both said: Al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How much of the month has passed? He said: We said: Twenty-two have passed and eight remain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, rather twenty-two of it have passed and seven remain. Seek it tonight. Yala said in his hadith: The month is twenty-nine."
"7418","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, or from Abu Said, he doubted, meaning al-Amash, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has roaming angels on the earth, extra besides the writers of men. When they find people remembering Allah they call out: Come to what you seek. So they come and surround them up to the lowest heaven. Then Allah says: What did you leave My servants doing? They say: We left them praising You and glorifying You and remembering You. He says: Have they seen Me? They say: No. He says: How would it be if they had seen Me? They say: If they had seen You they would have been more intense in praise and glorification and remembrance. He says: What do they seek? They say: They seek Paradise. He says: Have they seen it? They say: No. He says: How would it be if they had seen it? They say: If they had seen it they would have been more eager for it and more seeking of it. He said: He says: From what do they seek refuge? They say: From the Fire. He says: Have they seen it? They say: No. He said: He says: How would it be if they had seen it? They say: If they had seen it they would have been more fleeing from it and more fearing of it. He said: He says: I call you to witness that I have forgiven them. He said: They say: Among them is so-and-so, the sinner, who did not intend them but came only for a need. He says: They are the people whose companion is not wretched through them."
"7419","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah, and he did not raise it, similar to it."
"7420","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us from his father from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has traveling angels, extra, who seek gatherings of remembrance. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"7421","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr said: al-Amash informed us, from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a believer of a distress among the distresses of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress among the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. Whoever covers a Muslim, Allah will cover him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever eases for one in hardship, Allah will ease for him in this world and the Hereafter. Allah is in the aid of the servant so long as the servant is in the aid of his brother. Whoever travels a path seeking knowledge in it, Allah will make easy for him thereby a path to Paradise. No people gather in a house among the houses of Allah reciting the Book of Allah and studying it among themselves except tranquility descends upon them and mercy covers them and the angels surround them and Allah the Mighty and Majestic mentions them among those with Him. Whoever is slowed by his work, his lineage will not hasten him."
"7422","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters, he will have two rewards. He said: So I narrated them to Kab. Kab said: There is no reckoning upon him nor upon an abstemious believing believer."
"7423","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is what leaves sufficiency. Your wife says: Feed me or divorce me. Your servant says: Feed me or sell me. Your child says: To whom do you entrust me? They said: O Abu Hurayrah, is this something the Messenger of Allah said or is this from your own pocket? He said: Rather this is from my own pocket."
"7424","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of a man in congregation exceeds his prayer in his house and his prayer in his market by twenty and some degrees. That is because when one of you performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then comes to the mosque intending only prayer, nothing urges him except prayer, he does not take a step except a degree is raised for him thereby and a sin is removed from him thereby, until he enters the mosque. When he enters the mosque he is in prayer so long as prayer detains him, and the angels pray upon one of you so long as he remains in the sitting place in which he prayed, saying: O Allah forgive him, O Allah have mercy on him, O Allah turn to him, so long as he does not harm therein, so long as he does not break ablution therein."
"7425","Abd Allah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cancels a stumble, Allah will cancel his on the Day of Resurrection."
"7426","Abu Muawiyah and Yala both said: Al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you. They are softer in hearts and more tender in minds. Faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni. Abu Muawiyah said, meaning in his hadith: The head of disbelief is toward the east."
"7427","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spoils were not made lawful for dark-headed people before you. Fire used to descend from the sky and consume it. On the day of Badr people hastened to the spoils, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took. So eat from what you gained, lawful and good."
"7428","Abu Muawiyah and Waki both said: Al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever obeys the commander, and Waki said: the imam, has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the commander has disobeyed me, and Waki said: the imam, has disobeyed me."
"7429","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group of my community to enter Paradise will be upon the image of the moon on the night of full moon. Then those who follow them upon the brightest star in the sky in light. Then after that ranks. They will not defecate nor urinate nor blow their noses nor spit. Their combs are gold, their sweat is musk, their censers are aloeswood. Their character is upon the character of one man, upon the height of their father, sixty cubits."
"7430","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the thief who steals an egg and his hand is cut, and steals a rope and his hand is cut."
"7431","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced continuous fasting, so he forbade them. He said: I am not like you. I spend the day with my Lord Who feeds me and gives me drink."
"7432","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes in the night, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"7433","He said: And Waki said from Abu Salih and Abu Razin from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, three times. Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Until he washes it once or twice."
"7434","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: At the back of the head of one of you is a rope with three knots. When he wakes and remembers Allah a knot is untied. When he stands and performs ablution a knot is untied. When he stands for prayer all his knots are untied. He said: So he wakes energetic, good in soul, having attained good. If he does not do so he wakes lazy, foul in soul, having attained no good."
"7435","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three, Allah will not speak to them nor look at them nor purify them, and theirs is a painful punishment: a man with surplus water in the desert who withholds it from the traveler, a man who pledges to the imam pledging him only for worldly gain, if he is given of it he fulfills to him and if he is not given he does not fulfill to him. He said: And a man who sells a man goods after the afternoon prayer, swearing to him by Allah that he took it for such-and-such, so he believes him while it is otherwise."
"7436","Abu Muawiyah and Waki and Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Al-Amash narrated to us, and Ibn Numayr: Al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No child is born except upon this creed. And Waki once said: Upon the creed."
"7437","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us who said: I heard my father from Abu Hamzah from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No child is born except upon this creed, then his parents make him Jewish and make him Christian. Then he mentioned similar to it."
"7438","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us from al-Amash from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No child is born except upon this creed until his tongue expresses from him. Then his parents make him Jewish or make him Christian or make him associate. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what about what was before that? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"7439","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No wealth ever benefited me as the wealth of Abu Bakr benefited me. So Abu Bakr wept and said: Am I and my wealth except for you, O Messenger of Allah?"
"7440","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih and Abu Razin from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. And when the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in his other sandal until he repairs it."
"7441","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with an iron, his iron is in his hand stabbing himself in his belly in the fire of Hell, abiding therein forever. Whoever kills himself with poison, his poison is in his hand sipping it in the fire of Hell, abiding therein forever. Whoever throws himself from a mountain and kills himself, he is falling in the fire of Hell, abiding therein forever."
"7442","Abu Muawiyah and Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look to whoever is below you and do not look to whoever is above you, for it is more fitting that you not scorn the blessing of Allah. Abu Muawiyah said: Upon you."
"7443","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, or from Abu Said, he doubted, meaning al-Amash, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has freed ones in every day and night. For each servant among them there is an answered supplication."
"7444","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us who said: My father, and he is the brother of Ismail ibn Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, who said: My father, and he was preferred over his brother, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from Said ibn Abi Said from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May the nose of a man be dusted who is mentioned before me and does not send prayers upon me. May the nose of a man be dusted upon whom Ramadan enters and ends before he is forgiven. May the nose of a man be dusted who reaches his parents in old age and they do not admit him to Paradise. Ribi said: I know only that he said: Or one of them."
"7445","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans with stones, let him make it odd."
"7446","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay by the rich is injustice. When one of you is transferred to a solvent one, let him follow."
"7447","Ribi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abu al-Zinad narrated to us from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it, woe to you."
"7448","Ribi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Dinar from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Irak ibn Malik from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no charity upon the Muslim in his horse nor his slave."
"7449","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Muslim ibn Abi Muslim who said: I saw Abu Hurayrah when we were boys, the Bedouins coming, saying: O Bedouin, we will sell for you. He said: Leave him to sell his goods. Then Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a town-dweller to sell for a desert-dweller."
"7450","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Abu Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The unattended animal, its wound is void, and the well is void, and the mine is void, and in buried treasure is a fifth."
"7451","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ali, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us from Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, Abu Hurayrah narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a unit of the morning prayer before the sun rises has not missed it, and whoever prays a unit of the afternoon prayer before the sun sets has not missed it."
"7452","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us who said: I heard al-Hasan who said: Abu Hurayrah said: Three my close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me which I never leave: the odd prayer before I sleep, fasting three days of every month, and washing on Friday."
"7453","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a unit of the afternoon before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches it of the morning before the sun rises has caught it."
"7454","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar and al-Thawri narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Abu Amr ibn Hurayth from his father from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, who said: When one of you prays, let him pray toward something. If there is nothing, then a stick. If there is no stick, let him draw a line. Then whatever passes in front of him will not harm him."
"7455","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Ibn Awn from Umayr ibn Ishaq who said: I was with al-Hasan ibn Ali when Abu Hurayrah met us. He said: Show me that I may kiss from you where I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss. He said: He said: With the shirt? He said: So he kissed his navel."
"7456","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Yahya from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married upon her paternal aunt nor upon her maternal aunt."
"7457","Abu Qatan and Abu Amir both said: Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwai, narrated to us from Yahya from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: By Allah I shall bring you close to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Abu Hurayrah used to supplicate in the last unit of the noon prayer and the night prayer and the morning prayer. Abu Amir said in his hadith: The last night prayer and the morning prayer, after saying: Allah hears whoever praises Him, supplicating for the believers and cursing the disbelievers. And Abu Amir said: And cursing the disbelievers."
"7458","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Said ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he intended to supplicate against someone or supplicate for someone, supplicated after bowing. Perhaps he said when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, to You is praise: O Allah save al-Walid ibn al-Walid and Salamah ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah and the oppressed among the believers. O Allah press hard Your tread upon Mudar and make them years like the years of Yusuf. He said: He said that aloud, and he says in some of his prayers, in the dawn prayer: O Allah curse so-and-so and so-and-so, two tribes of the Arabs, until Allah the Mighty and Majestic revealed: You have nothing of the affair, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"7459","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Yahya from Ikrimah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you prays in a single garment, let him oppose between its two ends over his shoulders."
"7460","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is below the waist-wrapper is in the Fire."
"7461","Al-Khaffaf narrated to us from Abu Yaqub. [Source text truncated; no matn present.]"
"7462","Yazid narrated to us, Said narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Bashir ibn Nahik from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever has a share in a slave and frees half of him, upon him is his full release if he has wealth. If he has no wealth, the slave is asked to earn the price of his neck without hardship."
"7463","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us from Yahya from Damdam from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded killing the two black ones in prayer. Yahya said: The two black ones are the snake and the scorpion."
"7464","Yazid narrated to us, Misar informed us from Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Overlooked for my community is what their selves speak of or whisper, so long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."
"7465","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us from Qatadah, and Ibn Jafar: Shubah narrated to us who said: I heard Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the woman spends the night abandoning her husband's bed, the angels curse her. Ibn Jafar said: Until she returns."
"7466","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: In Friday there is an hour. And Ibn Awn made us see with his right palm. We said: Belittling it. No Muslim man standing praying, asking Allah for good, but He gives it to him."
"7467","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us from Abu al-Walid and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad together from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell. When heat is intense, cool the prayer."
"7468","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us from Abu al-Walid from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you lead, lighten, for among you are the old and the weak and the young."
"7469","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us from Muslim ibn Jundub from Habib al-Hudhali from Abu Hurayrah who said: If I saw a mountain goat roaming between its two lava tracts, meaning Medina, I would not frighten it nor touch it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding its trees to be beaten or cut."
"7470","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The angels curse one of you when he points to his brother with iron, even if he is his full brother. My father said: Ibn Abi Adi did not raise it."
"7471","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us from al-Julas from Uthman ibn Shammas who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah when Marwan passed him. He said: Some of your hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or: your hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he returned. We said: Now he will attack him. He said: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray over funerals? He said: I heard him say: You created it and You provided it and You guided it to Islam and You took its soul. You know its secret and its open. We came as intercessors, so forgive it."
"7472","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, informed us from Ziyad al-Makhzumi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Kisra after Kisra and no Caesar after Caesar. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, their treasures shall surely be spent in the path of Allah."
"7473","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail informed us from Ziyad al-Makhzumi from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall enter Paradise by his work. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me from Him with mercy and bounty. And he placed his hand upon his head."
"7474","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Safwan ibn Abi Yazid from Husayn ibn al-Lajlaj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell do not gather in the nostrils of a Muslim man, nor do miserliness and faith gather in the heart of a Muslim man."
"7475","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us who said: I heard Salman Abu Abd Allah al-Agharr from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."
"7476","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us from Abu al-Hakam, freedman of the Laythians, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prize except in a light-footed camel or a hoof."
"7477","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the miser and the spender is like two men wearing two cloaks of iron from their breasts to their collarbones. As for the spender, he does not spend of it except a ring expands in its place, widening it upon him. As for the miser, it only increases upon him in tightness."
"7478","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah who said: Abu al-Qasim said: If Uhud were gold with me it would please me to spend it in the path of Allah and that three days come with nothing of it, dinar nor dirham, left with me except something I set aside for a debt upon me."
"7479","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My parable and the parable of the prophets before me is like a man who built a building and beautified it and completed it except for the place of a brick in a corner of its corners. People began to circle it and admire it and say: We never saw a building better than this except for the place of this brick. So I was this brick."
"7480","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Iyad ibn Dinar from his father that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group of my community to enter Paradise will be upon the image of the moon on the night of full moon, and the one after it upon the brightest star in the sky in light. And in Friday there is an hour no Muslim servant standing praying, asking Allah in it for something, but He gives it to him. Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour shall not rise until knowledge is taken and tribulations appear and harj abounds. They said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing."
"7481","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, Iyad ibn Dinar al-Laythi, and he was trustworthy, narrated to me from his father who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah addressing the people on Friday as the deputy of Marwan ibn al-Hakam over Medina in the days of pilgrimage, saying: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group. And he mentioned the hadith."
"7482","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Said ibn Yasar, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, that one of you take his rope and go to the mountain and collect firewood, then bring it carrying it upon his back and sell it and eat, is better for him than asking people. And that he take dust and put it in his mouth is better for him than putting in his mouth what Allah has forbidden to him."
"7483","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has angels who succeed one another, the angels of the night and the angels of the day. They gather in the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer. Then those who were among you ascend to Him. He asks them, and He knows best. He says: How did you leave My servants? They say: We left them praying and we came to them praying."
"7484","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah, and from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield. When one of you is fasting a day, let him not utter foul speech nor act ignorantly. If a man fights him or reviles him, let him say: I am fasting, I am fasting."
"7485","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the breath of the mouth of the fasting one is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic says: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is for Me and I reward for it. He leaves his food and his drink for Me, so his fasting is for him and I reward for it. Every good deed is ten like it up to seven hundred folds except fasting, for it is for Me and I reward for it."
"7486","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Musa ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah, and from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of continuous fasting. They said: But you practice continuous fasting, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I am not in that like you. I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. So undertake of deeds what you have capacity for."
"7487","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are mines. You find the best of them in ignorance the best of them in Islam when they understand."
"7488","Yazid narrated to me, Muhammad informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim eats in one intestine and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"7489","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it."
"7490","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you knew what I know you would weep much and laugh little."
"7491","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah decreed creation He wrote in His Book, and it is with Him above the Throne: My mercy precedes My anger."
"7492","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me with what I left you, for those before you perished only by their questioning and differing over their prophets. When I forbid you a thing, avoid it, and when I command you a thing, do of it what you can."
"7493","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us from Abu al-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names, a hundred minus one. Whoever enumerates them shall enter Paradise. He is Odd and loves the odd."
"7494","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us from Ata who said: Abu Hurayrah said: Every prayer in which recitation is made, what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made us hear we make you hear, and what he concealed from us we conceal from you."
"7495","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Muslim al-Qurashi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"7496","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Aqil ibn Maqil informed us from Hammam ibn Munabbih who said: I came to Medina and saw a circle at the pulpit of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I asked and was told: Abu Hurayrah. He said: So I asked. He said to me: From whom are you? I said: From the people of Yemen. He said: I heard my beloved, or he said: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni. They are softest in hearts. Harshness is among the loud-voiced herders of fur. And he pointed with his hand toward the east."
"7497","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a funeral. When I walked he outpaced me so I hurried, and when I hurried I outpaced him. I turned to a man beside me and said: The earth is folded for him, by the close friend of Ibrahim."
"7498","Yazid narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm informed him that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz informed him that Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever finds his property intact with a man who has gone bankrupt, or with a man who has gone bankrupt, he is more entitled to it than others."
"7499","Yazid narrated to us, Zakariyya informed us from Sad ibn Ibrahim from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"7500","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, and Abd al-Wahhab: Hisham informed us, from Yahya from Abu Jafar that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a third of the night remains, Allah the Mighty and Majestic descends to the lowest heaven and says: Who is it who calls Me that I answer him? Who is it who seeks My forgiveness that I forgive him? Who is it who seeks provision from Me that I provide him? Who is it who seeks removal of harm that I remove it from him? Until dawn breaks."
"7501","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya, from Abu Jafar, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three supplications are answered, there is no doubt about them: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of the father against his child."
"7502","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya, from Abu Jafar, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best deeds before Allah are faith in which there is no doubt, and fighting in which there is no misappropriation of spoils, and an accepted Hajj. Abu Hurairah said: An accepted Hajj expiates the sins of that year."
"7503","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad narrated to us, from Khalaf ibn Mihran, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asamm say: Abu Hurairah said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, the Duha prayer, and not to sleep except upon Witr."
"7504","Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad, a Kufan, trustworthy, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my ummah, I would have commanded them at every prayer to perform ablution, or with every ablution to use the siwak, and I would have delayed the last Isha prayer until a third of the night."
"7505","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the servant of one of you prepares his food for him and spares him its heat and its cold, let him seat him with him, and if he refuses then let him hand him a morsel in his hand."
"7506","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The prayer was called, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and stood in his place of prayer, then he remembered that he had not performed ghusl, so he left, then he said: Remain as you are. So we formed rows, and his head was dripping, and he led us in prayer."
"7507","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see the crescent then fast, and when you see it then break the fast, and if it is obscured from you then fast thirty days."
"7508","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you rises at night, let him not dip his hand into his vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"7509","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say the wretchedness of time, indeed Allah is al-Dahr, and do not name grapes al-Karm."
"7510","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Agharr Abu Abd Allah, the companion of Abu Hurairah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Friday comes, the angels sit at the doors of the mosque and write those who come to Friday, and when the imam comes out, the angels fold the scrolls and enter to listen to the remembrance."
"7511","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The early comer to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a sheep, then like one who offers a duck, then like one who offers a chicken, then like one who offers an egg."
"7512","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"7513","Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Who is more unjust than one who creates like My creation, then let them create a mosquito, or let them create an atom."
"7514","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Jibril kept enjoining me regarding the neighbor until I thought that he would make him an heir."
"7515","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Awf, from Khilas ibn Amr and Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever buys a milch she-camel that has been left unmilked or a ewe that has been left unmilked and milks it, then he has the choice by one of the two considerations until he keeps it or returns it, along with a vessel of food."
"7516","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Awf, from Khilas, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The likeness of one who takes back his gift is like the likeness of the dog that eats until when it is full it vomits, then it returns to its vomit and eats it."
"7517","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Awf, from Khilas, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should urinate in standing water and then perform ablution from it."
"7518","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurairah, the like thereof."
"7519","Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The orphan girl is to be consulted regarding herself; if she remains silent then that is her permission, and if she refuses then there is no marriage against her will."
"7520","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Allah created the creation, He wrote a book, and it is with Him above the Throne: My mercy has preceded My anger."
"7521","Ali ibn Hafs narrated to us, Warqa informed us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Fire is veiled with desires, and Paradise is veiled with disliked hardships."
"7522","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abu Mawdud informed me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hadrad narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you spits in the mosque, let him bury it, and if he does not do so then let him spit in his garment."
"7523","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Take my name but do not take my kunyah."
"7524","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, from al-Salt ibn Ghalib al-Hujaymi, from Muslim, who asked Abu Hurairah about drinking while standing, he said: O son of my brother, I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with his mount made to kneel and hobbled while I was holding its halter or its reins and placing my foot upon its foreleg, then a group of Quraysh came and stood around him, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a vessel of milk and he drank while he was upon his mount, then he passed it to the one next to him on his right, and he drank standing, until all the people drank standing."
"7525","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, or Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Does not he who raises his head while the imam is prostrating fear that Allah will transform his head into the head of a donkey."
"7526","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What ensures one who raises his head before the imam, while he is with the imam, that Allah will not transform his form into the form of a donkey."
"7527","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurairah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, and Witr before sleep, and ghusl on Friday."
"7528","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurairah, he said: They mentioned before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a man, or a man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so slept last night and did not pray until morning. He said: Satan urinated in his ear."
"7529","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever catches a rakah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches a rakah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets has caught it."
"7530","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The poor person is not the one whom a date or two dates, and a morsel or two morsels, turn away. They said: Then who is the poor person, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The one who finds no sufficiency, and people do not know his need so that charity is given to him. Al-Zuhri said: And that is the deprived one."
"7531","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with the like of this hadith, except that he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, then who is the poor person. He said: The one who has no sufficiency and does not beg people importunately."
"7532","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, the brother of Wahb, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Delaying payment by the rich is injustice."
"7533","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The Jews and the Christians do not dye, so differ from them."
"7534","Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People are like mines; the best of them in Jahiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they understand."
"7535","Ibn Numayr and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Four rivers burst forth from Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile, Sayhan, and Jayhan."
"7536","Yazid and Ibn Numayr said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Change grey hair, and do not resemble the Jews nor the Christians."
"7537","Yazid and Ibn Numayr said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand upon the Sirat, and it will be said: O people of Paradise. So they will look out, fearful and apprehensive of being removed, and Yazid said: of being removed from their place in which they are. Then it will be said: Do you know this. They will say: Yes, our Lord, this is death. Then it will be said: O people of the Fire. So they will look out, rejoicing and glad at being removed from their place in which they are. Then it will be said: Do you know this. They will say: Yes, this is death. Then the command will be given for it and it will be slaughtered upon the Sirat, then it will be said to both groups: Eternity in what you find, there is no death therein ever."
"7538","Yazid informed us, Muhammad, and Ibn Numayr said: Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat which she tied up and did not feed it, nor give it to drink, nor let it go so that it could eat from the vermin of the earth."
"7539","Ibn Numayr and Yazid said: Muhammad informed us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade continuous fasting. They said: You practice continuous fasting. He said: You are not like me; indeed Allah feeds me and gives me to drink. And Yazid said: I spend the night, my Lord feeds me and gives me to drink."
"7540","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Hanzalah, he said: I heard Salim, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Knowledge will be taken away, tribulations will appear, and harj will increase. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is harj. He said: Killing."
"7541","Yala narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Glorifying Allah is for men, and clapping is for women."
"7542","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When one of you prays and then sits in his place of prayer, the angels keep saying: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy upon him, so long as he does not break his ablution or stand up."
"7543","Yala and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Yazid said: They passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a funeral, and they praised it with good, among the traits of good, and he said: It has become due. Then another funeral passed by him, and they spoke of it with evil, among the traits of evil, and he said: It has become due. Then he said: You are witnesses on earth."
"7544","Yala and Yazid said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen the truth; indeed Satan does not resemble me."
"7545","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Euphrates will recede from a mountain of gold, and people will fight over it, and nine of every ten will be killed."
"7546","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Richness is not from abundance of possessions, but richness is the richness of the soul."
"7547","Yala and Yazid said: Muhammad informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: People follow Quraysh in this matter; their best follow their best, and their worst follow their worst."
"7548","Yazid and Yala said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said regarding the black seed: There is healing in it from every disease except al-Sam. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Sam. He said: Death."
"7549","Yala narrated to us, Fudayl, meaning Ibn Ghazwan, narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Num, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Silver for silver, like for like, weight for weight, and gold for gold, weight for weight, like for like; whoever increases, then that is usury. And fruit is not to be sold until its ripeness appears."
"7550","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three things are from the deeds of the people of Jahiliyyah which the people of Islam will not abandon: wailing, seeking rain by the stars, and such. And I said to Said: What is it. He said: The call of Jahiliyyah: O family of so-and-so, O family of so-and-so, O family of so-and-so."
"7551","Ribi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sends blessings upon me one time, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, writes for him ten good deeds thereby."
"7552","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sends blessings upon me one time, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, writes for him ten good deeds thereby."
"7553","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no owner of a hoard who does not pay its due except that it will be made into plates heated upon them in the Fire of Hell, and his forehead, his side, and his back will be branded with them, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of sheep who does not pay their due except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest number, and he will be laid out for them on a wide flat plain, and they will butt him with their horns and trample him with their hooves; there will be no hornless one among them nor one with broken horns; whenever the last of them passes, the first of them will be returned upon him, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who does not pay their due except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection in their fullest number, and he will be laid out for them on a wide flat plain, and they will trample him with their feet; whenever the last of them passes, the first of them will be returned upon him, until Allah judges between His servants on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years of what you count, then he will see his path, either to Paradise or to the Fire. Then he was asked about horses, and he said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, and they are a reward for a man, and a covering and beauty for a man, and a burden upon a man. As for the one for whom they are a reward, it is a man who keeps them, preparing them in the path of Allah, so whatever they conceal in their bellies is a reward for him, and if they pass by a river and drink from it, then whatever they conceal in their bellies is a reward for him, and if they pass by and eat from it, then that is a reward for him, and if they run restively upon an elevated land, then for every step they take there is a reward for him, until he mentioned their dung and their urine. And as for the one for whom they are a covering and beauty, it is a man who keeps them for honor and adornment, and does not forget the right of their bellies and their backs, in hardship and in ease. And as for the one upon whom they are a burden, it is a man who keeps them for extravagance, insolence, show, and arrogance. Then he was asked about donkeys, and he said: Nothing was revealed to me about them except this unique comprehensive verse: Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it."
"7554","Abu Kamil and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl, Affan said in his hadith: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, informed us, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour will not come until people are rained upon with a rain from which houses of mud-brick give no shelter, and nothing will give shelter from it except houses of hair."
"7555","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Iraq has withheld its qafiz and its dirham, and Syria has withheld its mudd and its dinar, and Egypt has withheld its irdabb and its dinar, and you have returned to where you began, and you have returned to where you began, and you have returned to where you began. The flesh of Abu Hurairah and his blood bear witness to that. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard Yahya ibn Main, and he mentioned Abu Kamil, and he said: I used to take from him this matter, and Abu Kamil was a Baghdadi from al-Abna."
"7556","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The angels do not accompany a party in which there is a dog or a bell."
"7557","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you meet them on the road, do not initiate the greeting with them, and force them to its narrowest part. Zuhayr said: So I said to Suhayl: The Jews and the Christians. He said: The polytheists."
"7558","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a man stands from his sitting place and then returns to it, he is more entitled to it."
"7559","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sleeps with grease on his hand and does not wash it, then something befalls him, let him blame none but himself."
"7560","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No child can repay his father except that he finds him enslaved and buys him and frees him."
"7561","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"7562","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure."
"7563","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhazzim, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, or Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, to let down the hem an arm's length."
"7564","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When the servant obeys his Lord and obeys his master, he has two rewards."
"7565","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One who killed a disbeliever and then remained upright after him will not be gathered together in the Fire."
"7566","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from a man, from Abu Hurairah, that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the hardness of his heart, and he said to him: If you want to soften your heart, then feed the poor and wipe the head of the orphan."
"7567","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Fasting the month of patience and fasting three days of every month is the fasting of a lifetime."
"7568","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim and Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should wish for death; either a doer of good, perhaps he may increase in good, or a doer of evil, perhaps he may seek to make amends."
"7569","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There was a man who used to lend to people, and he used to say to his servant: When you come to one in hardship, then overlook him, perhaps Allah will overlook us. He said: Then he met Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and He overlooked him."
"7570","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Our stopping place tomorrow, Allah willing, is at Khayf Bani Kinanah, where they swore together upon disbelief."
"7571","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see the crescent then fast, and when you see it then break the fast, and if it is obscured from you then fast thirty days."
"7572","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from al-Agharr and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, and Yaqub said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Agharr, from Abu Hurairah, and Yaqub did not mention Abu Salamah, my father said: Yunus narrated it to us, from al-Agharr and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When Friday comes, there are angels at every door among the doors of the mosque who write the first then the first, and when the imam sits, they fold the scrolls and come to listen to the remembrance."
"7573","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, and Yaqub narrated to us, my father, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurairah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever eats of this tree, let him not harm us with it in this mosque of ours. Yaqub said: Meaning garlic."
"7574","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Ibrahim said: I do not know it except from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, my father said: And Yaqub did not doubt, he said: The excellence of the congregational prayer over the prayer of one of you alone is twenty-five parts."
"7575","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet said: I was sent with comprehensive speech, and I was aided with terror, and while I was sleeping I was brought the keys of the treasuries of the earth and placed in my hand."
"7576","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Two men reviled one another, a man from the Muslims and a man from the Jews. So the Muslim said: By Him who chose Muhammad above the worlds. And the Jew said: By Him who chose Musa above the worlds. So the Muslim became angry and struck the eye of the Jew. Then the Jew came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of that. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called him and asked him, and he admitted it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not prefer me over Musa, for people will fall unconscious on the Day of Resurrection and I will be the first to recover, and I will find Musa holding to the side of the Throne, and I will not know whether he was among those who fell unconscious and recovered before me, or whether he was among those whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, exempted."
"7577","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Ubayd, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The deed of none of you will admit him to Paradise. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Not even me, except that Allah envelops me with bounty and mercy from Him."
"7578","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Adam and Musa argued, peace be upon them both. So Musa said to him: You are Adam whose sin expelled you from Paradise. So Adam said to him: And you are Musa whom Allah chose with His speech and with His message, you blame me for a matter decreed upon me before I was created. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: So Adam overcame Musa, so Adam overcame Musa."
"7579","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, that Abu Hurairah said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, then he mentioned the hadith."
"7580","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: Which deeds are best. He said: Faith in Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then what. He said: Then jihad in the path of Allah. It was said: Then what. He said: Then an accepted Hajj."
"7581","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to say: O Muslim women, let not a neighbor woman belittle a gift to her neighbor, even a sheep's foot."
"7582","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from al-Agharr and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Our Lord, Blessed is His Name, descends every night when the last third of the night remains to the lowest heaven, and says: Who calls upon Me that I may answer him, who asks Me that I may give him, who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him, until dawn rises. That is why they used to prefer prayer at the end of the night over prayer at its beginning."
"7583","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I came to Said ibn Marjanah and asked him, and he said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays over a funeral and does not walk with it, let him stand until it disappears from him, and whoever walks with it, let him not sit until it is set down."
"7584","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever catches a rakah of the prayer has caught it."
"7585","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, one who heard Abu Hurairah narrated to me, saying: My close friend enjoined upon me three things and forbade me three things: he enjoined upon me Witr before sleep, and fasting three days of every month, and the two rakahs of Duha. He said: And he forbade me turning around, and squatting like the squatting of the monkey, and pecking like the pecking of the rooster."
"7586","Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn al-Sammak narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, one who heard Abu Hurairah narrated to me, saying: My close friend, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enjoined upon me fasting three days of every month, and Witr before sleep, and the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the oft-returning."
"7587","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurairah, raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah says: One whose two beloved eyes I take away, and he is patient and expects reward, I am not content with a reward for him less than Paradise."
"7588","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Layth, from Kab, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you send blessings upon me, then ask Allah for me al-Wasilah. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Wasilah. He said: The highest degree in Paradise, which none will attain except one man, and I hope that I am he."
"7589","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed Allah loves sneezing and hates or dislikes yawning; when one of them says ha ha, that is only Satan laughing from inside him."
"7590","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you wakes up, let him not put his hand into his vessel, or he said: into his ablution water, until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"7591","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a mouse that falls into ghee, and he said: If it is solid, then throw it and what is around it, and if it is liquid, then do not approach it. Abd al-Razzaq said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Budhawayh informed me that Mamar used to mention it with this isnad, and mention, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. And he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurairah."
"7592","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: None of you should urinate in standing water and then perform ablution from it."
"7593","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. And he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When the dog laps in the vessel, then wash it seven times."
"7594","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, he said: I passed by Abu Hurairah while he was performing ablution, and he said: Do you know from what I perform ablution. From crumbs of aqit I ate. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"7595","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar and Ibn Jurayj informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, does a man pray in a single garment. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do all of you have two garments. He said in the hadith of Ibn Jurayj: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah narrated."
"7596","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every good deed the son of Adam does is multiplied tenfold to seven hundredfold, except fasting, for it is for Me and I reward for it; he leaves his desire for My sake and leaves his food for My sake. There are two joys for the fasting person: joy at his breaking the fast, and joy at the meeting with his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. And the breath of the fasting person's mouth is better with Allah than the scent of musk."
"7597","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays in a single garment, let him cross its two ends over his shoulder."
"7598","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it off with a stone or with something, then he said: When one of you stands for prayer, let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, for to his right is an angel, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"7599","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever eats of this tree, meaning garlic, let him not harm us in our mosque. And he said in another place: Let him not approach our mosque, nor harm us with the smell of garlic."
"7600","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abbad ibn Unays, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Indeed the muadhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and everything moist and dry that hears him confirms him, and the witness has twenty-five degrees."
"7601","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of congregational prayer over the prayer of a single person is twenty-five, and the angels of the night and the angels of the day gather together at the Fajr prayer. He said: Then Abu Hurayrah would say: And recite if you wish: And the recitation of dawn; indeed the recitation of dawn is witnessed."
"7602","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat intensifies, delay the prayer to cooler time, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"7603","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer as long as he is waiting for the prayer, and the angels continue to invoke blessings upon one of you as long as he is in the mosque, saying: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"7604","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar and al-Thawri narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Abu Amr ibn Hurayth, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it to the Prophet, who said: When one of you prays, let him pray toward something; if there is nothing, then a staff; if there is no staff, then let him draw a line; then whatever passes in front of him will not harm him."
"7605","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever peeks upon a people in their house without their permission, it has become permissible for them to gouge out his eye."
"7606","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not initiate the Jews and the Christians with the greeting of peace, and when you meet them on a road, force them to its narrowest part."
"7607","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no evil omen, and the best of it is optimism. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is optimism? He said: The good word one of you hears."
"7608","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no evil omen, and the best of it is optimism. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"7609","Abd al-Razzaq and Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Hamah. A Bedouin said: What about camels that are in the sand as if they were gazelles, then a mangy camel mixes with them and makes them mangy? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then who infected the first one?"
"7610","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever takes a dog, except a hunting dog or a farming dog or a livestock dog, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"7611","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and al-Agharr, the companion of Abu Hurayrah, informed me that Abu Hurayrah informed them, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, descends every night when the last third of the night remains, to the lowest heaven, and says: Who calls upon Me that I may answer him? Who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Who asks Me that I may give him?"
"7612","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred minus one; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. And Hammam added in it, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed He is Odd and loves the odd."
"7613","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: the rich are invited and the poor are left out, and it is a duty, and whoever abandons it has disobeyed. And Ma'mar would sometimes say: Whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"7614","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed when Allah loves a servant, He says to Jibril: I love so-and-so, so love him. He said: Then Jibril says to the inhabitants of heaven: Indeed your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him. He said: Then the inhabitants of heaven love him. He said: And acceptance is placed for him on earth. He said: And when He hates, then the like of that."
"7615","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."
"7616","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are more tender of hearts. Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and understanding is Yemeni."
"7617","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, that they heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best quarters of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Banu Abd al-Ashhal, and they are the clan of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then Banu al-Najjar. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then Banu Sa'idah. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then in every quarter of the Ansar there is good. Ma'mar said: Thabit and Qatadah informed me that they heard Anas ibn Malik mentioning this hadith, except that he said: Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal."
"7618","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, the freedman of Banu Jumah, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was strutting in a garment, admiring his thick hair, having let his lower garment trail, Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he is sinking in it - or he said: falling into it - until the Day of Resurrection."
"7619","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Thabit ibn Qays narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah said: A wind seized the people on the road to Makkah, while Umar ibn al-Khattab was performing Hajj, and it bore down heavily upon them. Umar said to those around him: Who will narrate to us about the wind? They did not return anything to him. The question Umar had asked about that reached me, so I urged my mount until I caught up with him, and I said: O Commander of the Believers, I was informed that you asked about the wind, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The wind is from the mercy of Allah; it comes with mercy and it comes with punishment. If you see it, do not revile it, and ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Him from its evil."
"7620","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been supported with awe, and I have been given the comprehensive speech, and while I was asleep, the keys of the treasures of the earth were brought and placed in my hands. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has gone, and you are extracting them."
"7621","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends two of a pair of his wealth in the path of Allah will be called from the gates of Paradise, and Paradise has gates: whoever was among the people of prayer will be called from the gate of prayer, and whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity, and whoever was among the people of jihad will be called from the gate of jihad, and whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of al-Rayyan. Abu Bakr said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, there is no necessity upon anyone from whichever of them he is called, so will anyone be called from all of them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, and I hope that you will be among them."
"7622","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant gives charity from wholesome earnings, Allah accepts it from him and takes it with His right hand and nurtures it, as one of you nurtures his foal or his young camel. A man may give a morsel in charity, and it grows in the hand of Allah - or he said: in the palm of Allah - until it becomes like a mountain. So give charity."
"7623","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa argued. Musa said to Adam: O Adam, you are the one who brought your offspring into the Fire. Adam said: O Musa, Allah chose you with His messengership and His speech, and sent down upon you the Torah; did you find that I was brought down? He said: Yes. He said: Then Adam overcame him in argument."
"7624","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Abu Salamah."
"7625","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists. He said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"7626","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying about al-Shuniz: Upon you is this black seed, for in it is healing from everything except al-Sam. He means death."
"7627","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of Paradise are opened every Monday and Thursday. Ma'mar said: And other than Suhayl said: And deeds are presented every Monday and Thursday, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forgives every servant who does not associate anything with Him, except the two who bear grudges against each other. Allah says to the angels: Leave these two until they reconcile."
"7628","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, and Abd al-A'la, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The strong is not the one who overcomes in wrestling. They said: Then who is the strong, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The one who controls himself at anger."
"7629","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deeds are best? He said: Faith in Allah. He said: Then what? He said: Jihad in the path of Allah. He said: Then what? He said: Then an accepted Hajj."
"7630","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: In the end of time, the dream of the believer will hardly lie, and the most truthful of you in dreams is the most truthful of you in speech. Dreams are of three kinds: the good dream is glad tidings from Allah, Mighty and Majestic; the dream in which a man converses with himself; and the dream of grief from Satan. If one of you sees a dream he dislikes, let him not narrate it to anyone, and let him stand and pray. Abu Hurayrah said: The shackle pleases me and I dislike the yoke; the shackle is steadfastness in religion. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"7631","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"7632","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Hassan said in a circle in which was Abu Hurayrah: I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Hurayrah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Answer on my behalf; may Allah support you with the Holy Spirit? He said: O Allah, yes."
"7633","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest."
"7634","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The angel of death was sent to Musa, and when he came to him he struck him and gouged out his eye. He returned to his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and said: You sent me to a servant who does not want death. He said: So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, restored his eye to him and said: Return to him and say to him: Place his hand on the back of a bull; for all his hand covers, for every hair a year. He said: O Lord, then what? He said: Then death. He said: Then now. Then he asked Allah to bring him near the Holy Land, a stone's throw. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been there, I would have shown you his grave beside the road beneath the red mound."
"7635","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, who said: Al-Zuhri said to me: Shall I not narrate to you two wondrous hadiths? Al-Zuhri said: From Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man exceeded upon himself, and when death came to him he enjoined his sons, saying: When I die, burn me, then grind me, then scatter me in the wind into the sea. By Allah, if my Lord gains power over me He will punish me with a punishment with which none has been punished. He said: They did that to him. Then Allah said to the earth: Render what you took, and there he was standing. He said: What carried you to what you did? He said: Your fear, O Lord - or: fear of You. So He forgave him for that. Al-Zuhri said: And Humayd narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat she tied up; she neither fed it nor let it go to eat from the vermin of the earth until it died. Al-Zuhri said: That is so that no man relies presumptuously, and no man despairs."
"7636","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, while al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Tamimi was sitting. Al-Aqra said: O Messenger of Allah, I have ten children; I have never kissed a single one of them. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him and said: Indeed whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"7637","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to Umm Hani bint Abi Talib. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old and I have dependents. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who have ridden are the women of Quraysh: the most affectionate toward a child in his childhood, and the most careful with a husband regarding his means. Abu Hurayrah said: And Maryam bint Imran never rode a camel."
"7638","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, except his saying: And Maryam never rode a camel."
"7639","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, or one of them, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pride and arrogance are among the loud-voiced owners of tents of the people of hair, and tranquility is among the people of sheep. Faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni."
"7640","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I have a right over Quraysh, and indeed Quraysh have a right over you: as long as they judge justly when they judge, and fulfill when they are entrusted, and show mercy when mercy is sought from them."
"7641","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"7642","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Hammam, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How excellent it is for the servant that Allah causes him to die while excelling in worship of his Lord and obedience to his master. How excellent for him, how excellent for him."
"7643","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, al-Zuhri informed me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."
"7644","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Abu Hurayrah used to lead us in prayer, and he would say takbir when he stood and when he bowed, and when he intended to prostrate after rising from bowing, and when he intended to prostrate after rising from prostration, and when he sat, and when he intended to rise in the two rak'ahs he said takbir, and he would say takbir likewise in the other two rak'ahs. When he gave salam, he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am the nearest of you in resemblance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning his prayer. This remained his prayer until he departed the world."
"7645","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, and from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that they prayed behind Abu Hurayrah, and they mentioned the like of the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq."
"7646","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood for prayer, would say takbir. Then he mentioned the like of it."
"7647","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray, say: Amin. For the angels say: Amin, and the imam says: Amin. Whoever's saying Amin coincides with the angels' saying Amin, his preceding sins are forgiven."
"7648","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, said: O Allah, our Lord, and to You belongs praise."
"7649","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, al-Zuhri said: And Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not come to it hastening, but come to it walking, while tranquility is upon you. What you catch, pray, and what you miss, complete."
"7650","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the prayer is established. Then he mentioned it."
"7651","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What you catch, pray, and what you miss, make up. Ma'mar said: And he did not mention prostration."
"7652","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever catches a rak'ah of the prayer has caught the prayer."
"7653","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr or Asr and gave salam after two rak'ahs. Dhu al-Shimalayn ibn Abd Amr, who was an ally of Banu Zuhrah, said to him: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying? They said: He spoke the truth, O Prophet of Allah. So he completed with them the two rak'ahs he had omitted."
"7654","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, or one of them, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him lighten it, for among them are the weak, the very old sheikh, and the one with a need."
"7655","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Can the one who raises his head before the imam feel secure from Allah turning his head into the head of a donkey?"
"7656","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head from the last rak'ah in the Fajr prayer, he said: O Allah, our Lord, and to You belongs praise. Save al-Walid and Salamah ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah and the oppressed among the believers. O Allah, harden Your grip upon Mudar and make it upon them like the years of Yusuf."
"7657","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not permitted anything as He has permitted a prophet to chant the Quran."
"7658","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to me, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things I will not abandon, neither in residence nor in travel: sleeping upon witr, fasting three days of every month, and the two rak'ahs of Duha. He said: Then al-Hasan became confused and put, in place of Duha, ghusl on Friday."
"7659","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sa'd, informed me, that Thabit ibn Iyad, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. He said: And he also informed me that Hilal ibn Usamah informed him that he heard Abu Salamah informing of that from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7660","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, and Ibn Bakr, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ziyad informed me, that Thabit, the freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd - and Ibn Bakr said: he informed him - that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is sleeping, then wakes up and intends wudu, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he pours upon his hand, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"7661","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Qariz informed him that he found Abu Hurayrah performing wudu on the back of the mosque. Abu Hurayrah said: I perform wudu only because of pieces of aqit I ate, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform wudu from what fire has touched."
"7662","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until a people fight you who wear hair as shoes, their faces like hammered shields."
"7663","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the buttocks of the women of Daws shake around Dhu al-Khalasah. And it was an idol Daws used to worship in the Jahiliyyah at Tabalah."
"7664","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kisra will go and there will be no Kisra after him, and Qaysar will go and there will be no Qaysar after him. By the One in whose hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the path of Allah, Exalted."
"7665","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, Ibn Maryam is about to descend among you as a just judge and an equitable imam; he will break the cross, kill the pig, abolish the jizyah, and wealth will overflow until no one accepts it."
"7666","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Nafi, the freedman of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when Ibn Maryam descends among you and leads you - or he said: your imam is from among you?"
"7667","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Hanzalah al-Aslami, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, Ibn Maryam will surely enter ihram from Fajj al-Rawha with Hajj or Umrah, or with both together."
"7668","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let none of you revile time, for Allah is time. And let none of you say for grapes al-karm, for al-karm is the Muslim man."
"7669","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: The son of Adam harms Me. He says: O disappointment of time. For I am time; I alternate its night and its day. If I wish, I seize them."
"7670","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Harith ibn Mukhallad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the one who approaches his wife in her anus, Allah does not look at him."
"7671","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear a man saying: The people have perished, he is the most ruined of them. Allah says: Indeed he is ruined."
"7672","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and Ibn Bakr, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If you say to your companion: Be quiet, while the imam is delivering the khutbah on Friday, you have engaged in idle talk. Ibn Bakr said in his hadith: He said: Ibn Shihab informed me of the hadith of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, and of the hadith of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it."
"7673","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub informed me, from Abu Abd Allah Ishaq, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun neither rises nor sets upon a day better than Friday. And there is no beast but that it is alarmed on Friday, except these two weights of jinn and men. At every gate of the mosque are two angels writing the first, then the first: like a man who offered a camel, and like a man who offered a cow, and like a man who offered a sheep, and like a man who offered a bird, and like a man who offered an egg. When the imam sits, the scrolls are folded."
"7674","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, al-Abbas narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah al-Ansari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed in Friday there is an hour no Muslim servant coincides with, asking Allah, Mighty and Majestic, therein for good, except He gives it to him. And it is after Asr."
"7675","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: From washing it is ghusl, and from carrying it is wudu."
"7676","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib informed me - and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Abd al-Malik - that Nafi ibn Jubayr informed him that Abu Hurayrah informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever prays over a funeral and follows it, for him are two qirats like Uhud twice over, and whoever prays and does not follow it, for him is a qirat like Uhud. Ibn Bakr said: The qirat is like Uhud."
"7677","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Muhammad ibn Amr, that he informed him that Salamah ibn al-Azraq was sitting with Abd Allah ibn Umar in the market, and a funeral passed by over which weeping was raised. Abd Allah ibn Umar disapproved of that and rebuked them. Salamah ibn al-Azraq said to him: Do not say that, for I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah that I heard him saying: A woman of the daughters-in-law of Marwan died, and he attended her, and Marwan ordered the women who were weeping to be driven away. Abu Hurayrah said: Leave them, O Abu Abd al-Malik, for a funeral over which weeping was raised passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was with him, and with him was Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar rebuked those who were weeping with the funeral. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave them, O Ibn al-Khattab, for the soul is afflicted, and the eye is tearful, and the covenant is recent. He said: Did you hear it? He said: Yes. He said: Then Allah and His Messenger know best."
"7678","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man who broke fast in Ramadan to free a neck, or fast two months, or feed sixty poor persons."
"7679","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me, from Abu Salih al-Zayyat, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is Mine and I reward for it. Fasting is a shield. When it is the fasting day of one of you, let him not be obscene that day nor raise his voice. If someone reviles him or fights him, let him say: I am a fasting man, twice. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk. The fasting person has two joys he rejoices in: when he breaks fast he rejoices in his breaking, and when he meets his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, he rejoices in his fasting."
"7680","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and confuses him until he does not know how much he prayed. If he finds that, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"7681","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Umar ibn Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me, that while he was sitting with Nafi ibn Jubayr, Abu Abd Allah, the in-law of Zayd ibn al-Rayyan - and Ibn Bakr said: Ibn al-Zabban - passed by them. Nafi called him and he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer with the imam is better than twenty-five prayers one prays alone."
"7682","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah informing them: In every prayer there is recitation. What the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us, we make audible to you, and what he concealed from us, we conceal from you. Ibn Bakr said: In every prayer there is Quran."
"7683","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I do not know it but from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Surplus water is not withheld that surplus herbage may thereby be withheld."
"7684","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a sheep whose milk has been left to collect, he milks it; if he is pleased with it he keeps it, and if not he returns it, and returns with it a sa of dates."
"7685","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Kathir informed me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sells a sheep or a milch camel, let him not leave its milk to collect in its udder."
"7686","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no town-dweller sell for a Bedouin, and do not practice najsh, and let no man outbid his brother, nor propose over his proposal, and let no woman ask for the divorce of her sister."
"7687","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a distressed person of a distress in this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress in the Hereafter. Whoever veils the nakedness of a Muslim in this world, Allah will veil his nakedness in the Hereafter. Allah is in the aid of a man as long as he is in the aid of his brother."
"7688","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you prevent his neighbor from placing a beam upon his wall. Then Abu Hurayrah says: What is wrong with me that I see you turning away? By Allah, I will surely cast it between your shoulders."
"7689","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Two women of Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw the other with a stone and struck her belly, killing her and causing her to miscarry a fetus. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged its blood money upon the aqilah, and for its fetus a ghurrah, a slave or a slave girl. A speaker said: How can blood money be paid for one who neither ate nor drank nor spoke nor cried out? The like of that is void. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, as Abu Hurayrah claimed: This is of the brethren of the soothsayers."
"7690","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The animal is jubar, the well is jubar, the mine is jubar, and in buried treasure is the fifth. And jubar is void."
"7691","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-A'raj, who said: Abu Hurayrah said: You say Abu Hurayrah narrates much from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah is the appointed place of meeting. You say: What is with the Muhajirun that they do not narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these hadiths, and what is with the Ansar that they do not narrate with these hadiths? My companions of the Muhajirun were kept busy by their dealings in the markets, and my companions of the Ansar were kept busy by their lands and attending to them. I was a man who kept close by, and I used to frequent the companionship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I attended when they were absent and I memorized when they forgot. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us one day and said: Whoever spreads his garment until I finish my hadith, then draws it to himself, will never forget anything he heard from me. So I spread my garment - or he said: my striped cloak - then I drew it to myself. By Allah, I have not forgotten anything I heard from him. By Allah, were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah I would never have narrated to you anything. Then he recited: Indeed those who conceal what We sent down of the clear proofs and the guidance, the whole verse."
"7692","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last, the first on the Day of Resurrection. We are the first of people to enter Paradise, except that they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. Allah guided us, by His permission, to what they differed about of the truth. This is the day Allah guided us to, and people are followers for us therein: tomorrow for the Jews and the day after tomorrow for the Christians."
"7693","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, except that they were given the Book before us and we were given it after them. This is their day that was obligated upon them, and they differed about it, so Allah guided us to it. They are followers for us therein: the Jews tomorrow and the Christians the day after tomorrow."
"7694","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no newborn but Satan touches him when he is born, and he begins crying out from Satan's touching him, except Maryam and her son. Then Abu Hurayrah says: Recite if you wish: And I seek refuge for her with You and her offspring from Satan the outcast."
"7695","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Abu Hurayrah used to narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who have ridden camels are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most affectionate toward a child in his childhood, and the most careful with a husband regarding his means. Abu Hurayrah said: And Maryam never rode a camel at all."
"7696","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Amr ibn Amir al-Khuza'i dragging his intestines - meaning the bowels - in the Fire, and he is the first who freed the sa'ibahs."
"7697","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Abu Urwah Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever repents before the sun rises from its west, it is accepted from him."
"7698","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitrah; his parents make him Jewish and make him Christian and make him Magian, as livestock produce: do you sense among them any mutilated? Then he says: And recite if you wish: Allah's fitrah upon which He originated people; there is no change in Allah's creation."
"7699","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from a man of Banu Ghifar, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah has indeed removed excuse from a servant He kept alive until he reached sixty or seventy years. Allah has indeed removed excuse; Allah has indeed removed excuse from him."
"7700","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad informed me, who said: Abu Hurayrah and Ka'b gathered, and Abu Hurayrah began narrating to Ka'b from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ka'b narrating to Abu Hurayrah from the Books. Abu Hurayrah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every prophet there is an answered supplication, and I have kept my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"7701","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Sulayman ibn Dawud said: I shall surely go around tonight to one hundred women, each woman among them giving birth to a boy who will fight in the cause of Allah. He said: And he forgot to say: If Allah wills. So he went around them. He said: None of them gave birth except one, to half a human being. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had he said: If Allah wills, he would not have broken his oath, and it would have been a means of attaining his need."
"7702","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Allah Most High said: Let none of you say: O woe of time, for I am time; I turn its night and its day, and when I will, I seize them both."
"7703","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The people said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you suffer any harm in seeing the sun when there is no cloud beneath it? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. Then he said: Do you suffer any harm in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon when there is no cloud beneath it? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then you will see Him on the Day of Resurrection likewise. Allah will gather the people and say: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. So whoever used to worship the moon will follow the moon, and whoever used to worship the sun will follow the sun, and whoever used to worship the false gods will follow the false gods. And this nation will remain, with its hypocrites among it. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will come to them in a form other than the one they know, and will say: I am your Lord. They will say: We seek refuge with Allah from you; this is our place until our Lord comes to us, and when our Lord comes we shall recognize Him. He said: Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will come to them in the form they recognize, and will say: I am your Lord. They will say: You are our Lord, and they will follow Him. He said: And a bridge will be laid over Hell. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: And I shall be the first to cross it. And the plea of the messengers on that day will be: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. And on it are hooks like the thorns of al-sadan. Have you seen the thorns of al-sadan? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They are like the thorns of al-sadan, except that none knows the measure of their enormity but Allah Most High. They will snatch the people according to their deeds; among them is one destroyed by his deed, and among them is one lacerated and then saved. Until, when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has finished judging between the servants and intends to bring out of the Fire whomever He intends to have mercy on among those who used to testify that there is no god but Allah, He will command the angels to bring them out, and they will recognize them by the mark of the traces of prostration, and Allah has forbidden the Fire to consume the trace of prostration from the son of Adam. So they will bring them out, though they have been scorched, and water called the water of life will be poured over them, and they will sprout like the sprouting of the seed borne in the torrent. And there will remain a man turning his face toward the Fire, saying: O my Lord, its wind has poisoned me and its flame has burned me, so turn my face away from the Fire. He will keep calling upon Allah until He says: Perhaps if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else. He will say: No, by Your might, I shall not ask You for anything else. So He will turn his face away from the Fire. Then after that he will say: O my Lord, bring me near to the gate of Paradise. He will say: Did you not claim that you would not ask Me for anything else? Woe to you, O son of Adam, how treacherous you are. He will keep calling until He says: Perhaps if I grant you, you will ask Me for something else. He will say: No, by Your might, I shall not ask You for anything else, and he will give pledges and covenants that he will not ask for anything else. So He will bring him near to the gate of Paradise. When he draws near to it, Paradise will open wide for him, and when he sees what is in it of bliss and joy, he will remain silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent. Then he will say: O my Lord, admit me to Paradise. He will say: Did you not claim that you would not ask for anything else, and you gave your pledges and covenants that you would not ask Me for anything else? He will say: O my Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation. He will keep calling upon Allah until Allah laughs. When He laughs at him, He will permit him to enter it. When he is admitted, it will be said to him: Wish for such-and-such. So he will wish. Then it will be said: Wish for such-and-such. So he will wish, until his wishes are exhausted. Then it will be said to him: This is yours, and the like of it with it. He said: And Abu Said was sitting with Abu Hurayrah, not altering anything of his narration, until when he reached his saying: This is yours, and the like of it with it, Abu Said said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: This is yours, and ten times the like of it with it. Abu Hurayrah said: I memorized: And the like of it with it. Abu Hurayrah said: And that man is the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise."
"7704","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Paradise and the Fire argued. Paradise said: O my Lord, what is with me that none enters me except the poor of the people and their lowly? And the Fire said: What is with me that none enters me except the tyrants and the arrogant? So He said to the Fire: You are My punishment; I afflict through you whom I will. And He said to Paradise: You are My mercy; I bestow through you upon whom I will. And each one of you two shall have its fill. As for Paradise, Allah will originate for it whatever He wills. As for the Fire, they will be cast into it and it will say: Is there any more, until He places His foot in it; thereupon it will fill up, and parts of it will draw together, and it will say: Enough, enough, enough."
"7705","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I have not seen anything more resembling minor sins than what Abu Hurayrah reported from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has written for the son of Adam his share of unlawful intercourse, which he will inevitably attain. The unlawful intercourse of the eye is the glance, the unlawful intercourse of the tongue is speech, the soul wishes and desires, and the private part confirms that or denies it."
"7706","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no man who does not pay the zakah of his wealth but that plates of fire will be made for him on the Day of Resurrection, with which his forehead and his brow and his back will be branded, on a day whose measure is fifty thousand years. They trample him with their hooves - I think he said - and bite him with their mouths; the first of them returns upon the last of them, until judgment is passed between the people, then he will see his path. And if they were sheep, it will be likewise, except that they will gore him with their horns and trample him with their hooves."
"7707","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar said, al-Zuhri informed me, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has three children die before reaching the age of accountability, the Fire will not touch him except to fulfill the oath, meaning the passing over it."
"7708","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Salamah informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The Fire complained to its Lord and said: My Lord, parts of me have consumed other parts, so grant me relief. So He permitted it two breaths each year. The most severe cold you experience is from the bitter cold of Hell, and the most severe heat you experience is from the heat of Hell."
"7709","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: When the chapter When the help of Allah and the conquest comes was revealed, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the most tender-hearted. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni."
"7710","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri - and Ma'mar used to say: From Abu Hurayrah - then he said afterwards: From al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, concerning zakat al-fitr: Upon every free person and slave, male or female, young or old, poor or rich, a sa of dates or half a sa of wheat. Ma'mar said: And it reached me that al-Zuhri used to attribute it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"7711","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, from Abu al-Rabi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, enjoined upon me three things I shall never abandon: I shall not sleep except upon witr, the Duha prayer, and fasting three days of every month."
"7712","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the servant of one of you prepares his food, then brings it, having endured its heat and its smoke, let him seat him with him to eat. If the food is meager, little, let him place in his hand a morsel or two morsels."
"7713","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abu Said, the freedman of Abdallah ibn Amir, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not envy one another, do not engage in false bidding, do not hate one another, do not turn away from one another, and let none of you sell over the sale of his brother. Be servants of Allah, brothers. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him, nor forsake him, nor despise him. Piety is here - and he pointed with his hand to his chest three times. It is enough evil for a Muslim man to despise his Muslim brother. Everything of the Muslim is forbidden to the Muslim: his blood, his wealth, and his honor."
"7714","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Name yourselves after me but do not use my kunyah. I am Abu al-Qasim."
"7715","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not point you to that by which Allah expiates sins and raises ranks? Steps to the mosques, completing ablution thoroughly in disagreeable circumstances, and waiting for one prayer after another prayer; that is the station of guarding."
"7716","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you performs ablution, let him blow his nose, and when he cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."
"7717","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Odd and loves the odd."
"7718","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is Odd and loves the odd."
"7719","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except the Sacred Mosque."
"7720","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ata informed me that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, from Abu Hurayrah - or from Aishah - that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except the Sacred Mosque."
"7721","He said: Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdallah narrated it to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, and he mentioned a hadith. He said: And Ata informed me that Abu Salamah informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, from Aishah, and he mentioned it without doubt."
"7722","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa."
"7723","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by a man driving a sacrificial camel. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it. Abu Hurayrah said: I saw him keeping pace with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a sandal around its neck."
"7724","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If the people knew what is in the call to prayer and the first row, they would draw lots for them. If they knew what is in hastening early, they would race to it. If they knew what is in the night prayer and the dawn prayer, they would come to them even crawling. So I said to Malik: Is it disliked to say al-atamah? He said: Thus said the one who narrated to me."
"7725","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata informed me that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him, from Abu Hurayrah - or from Aishah - that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques, except al-Masjid al-Aqsa."
"7726","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdallah informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, and he mentioned a hadith. He said: And Ata informed me that Abu Salamah informed him, from Abu Hurayrah and from Aishah, and he mentioned it without doubt."
"7727","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best charity is that given from surplus wealth, and begin with those you support. The upper hand is better than the lower hand. I said to Ayyub: What is from surplus wealth? He said: From the surplus of your wealth."
"7728","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ashath ibn Abdallah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man may work the deeds of the people of goodness for seventy years, then when he makes his will he acts unjustly in it, so his record is sealed with an evil deed and he enters the Fire. And a man may work the deeds of the people of evil for seventy years, then act justly in his will, so his record is sealed with a good deed and he enters Paradise. He said: Then Abu Hurayrah would say: Recite if you wish: Those are the limits of Allah, up to His saying: A humiliating punishment."
"7729","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Hammam, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you persists stubbornly in an oath concerning his family, it is more sinful for him before Allah than the expiation he was commanded to make."
"7730","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Dawud, from a shaykh, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There will come upon you a time in which a man will be given the choice between incapacity and wickedness. Whoever reaches that time, let him choose incapacity over wickedness."
"7731","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, my father informed me, Mina informed us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, curse Himyar. He turned away from him. Then he came to him from another side, and he turned away from him, while he kept saying: Curse Himyar. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah have mercy on Himyar; their mouths are peace and their hands are food; people of security and faith."
"7732","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When one of you performs ablution, let him draw water into his nose, then blow it out. Whoever cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number."
"7733","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Amr ibn Shuayb informed me, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am in the desert for four or five months, and among us are women in childbed, menstruating women, and those in major impurity. What do you think? He said: Upon you is dust."
"7734","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you rises at night, let him open his prayer with two light rakahs."
"7735","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever is invited, let him respond. If he is not fasting, let him eat, and if he is fasting, let him pray and supplicate for them."
"7736","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The mouse is a transformed creature, by the sign that milk of milch camels is brought near to it and it does not taste it, while milk of sheep is brought near to it and it drinks it - or he said: eats it. Kab said to him: Is it something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: Has the Torah been revealed to me?"
"7737","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no fara and no atirah. The fara is the first offspring produced for them, which they would slaughter."
"7738","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the dubba, the muzaffat, the hantam, and the naqir."
"7739","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Kathir informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Wine comes from these two trees: the date-palm and the grapevine."
"7740","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, declared sacred what is between the two lava fields of Madinah. Abu Hurayrah said: Had I found gazelles between its two lava fields, I would not have frightened them. And he made around Madinah, twelve miles, a sanctuary."
"7741","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah informed me that he heard al-Qarrazz - and he was among the companions of Abu Hurayrah - claiming that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever intends its people with evil - meaning Madinah - Allah will melt him as salt melts in water."
"7742","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever has wealth and does not discharge its due, it will be made on the Day of Resurrection a bald serpent with two black spots, which will pursue him until it places its hand in his mouth, and it will keep gnawing at it until judgment is passed between the servants."
"7743","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar and Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Makhul, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: There is no charity due from the believer on his slave nor on his horse."
"7744","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was distributing dates from the dates of charity, with al-Hasan ibn Ali in his lap. When he finished, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, carried him on his shoulder, and his saliva flowed onto the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, raised his head, and there was a date in his mouth. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, put his hand in and pulled it out from him, then said: Do you not know that charity is not lawful for the family of Muhammad?"
"7745","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The previously married woman is to be consulted, and the virgin is to be asked permission. They said: And what is her permission, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Her silence."
"7746","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab - thus he said - from Abu Hurayrah, who said: He came - and he mentioned the hadith of the Fazari - from the Prophet: My wife has given birth to a black boy, while he was thereby hinting at disavowing him. So the Messenger of Allah said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors? He said: Red. He said: Is there a grey one among them? He said: Yes, among them are grey camels. He said: From what do you think that is? He said: I do not know; perhaps a strain drew it out. He said: And this one, perhaps a strain drew him out. And he did not permit him to disavow him."
"7747","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: A man from Muzaynah narrated to us, while we were with Ibn al-Musayyab, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"7748","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him. Then if he drinks, flog him. Then if he drinks, flog him. Then if he drinks a fourth time, kill him."
"7749","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone."
"7750","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj and Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: If you say to your companion, while the imam is preaching: Be silent, you have engaged in idle talk."
"7751","Ibn Jurayj said: And Ibn Shihab informed me, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdallah ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, the like of it."
"7752","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever catches a rakah of the prayer has caught the prayer."
"7753","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, al-Agharr Abu Abdallah, the companion of Abu Hurayrah, informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When Friday comes, the angels sit at the doors of the mosque, writing down everyone who comes to Friday. When the imam comes out, the angels fold the scrolls and enter to listen to the remembrance. He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The one who comes early to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a sheep, then like one who offers a chicken, then like one who offers - I think he said - an egg."
"7754","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdallah informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: And Abu Abdallah al-Agharr informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Friday comes, there is at every gate - and he mentioned it - and he did not doubt concerning the egg."
"7755","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Abdallah al-Agharr, the like of it."
"7756","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was on the pulpit, saying: On Friday there is an hour - and he gestured with his palm as though minimizing it - no Muslim servant coincides with it asking Allah for something but that He gives it to him."
"7757","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man called Abu Ishaq, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him take a bath."
"7758","Yunus narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from a man of Banu Layth, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him take a bath."
"7759","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I know it only as raised - the hadith - he said: Hasten with your funerals. If it was righteous, you hasten it to good, and if it was wicked, you find relief from it and lay it down from your necks."
"7760","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdallah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Ibn Abi Hafsah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said - and he mentioned its meaning. Abdallah narrated to us, he said: My father said: And Yunus differed from them both, saying: Abu Umamah ibn Sahl narrated to me."
"7761","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah."
"7762","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is placed in the grave has two qirats. And the two qirats are like two great mountains."
"7763","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, announced the death of al-Najashi to his companions while he was in Madinah. They lined up behind him, and he prayed over him, saying takbir four times."
"7764","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, that Abu Hurayrah used to prostrate in it. Abu Hurayrah said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating in it, meaning: When the heaven splits asunder."
"7765","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah - or from one of them - from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. If it is obscured from you, fast thirty days."
"7766","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade hastening the month of Ramadan with a fast of a day or two days, except a man who used to fast regularly, and that coincides with his fast."
"7767","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Abi Unays, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the month of Ramadan enters, the gates of mercy are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained."
"7768","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih - Ibn Shihab said: Ibn Abi Anas narrated to me that his father narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Ramadan enters, the gates of mercy are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained."
"7769","My father said: And Yaqub narrated it to us - my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, who said: It was mentioned that Ibn Shihab said: Ibn Abi Anas narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah - and he did not say: From his father - and he mentioned the hadith."
"7770","Attab narrated it to us, Abdallah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Ibn Abi Anas narrated to us, and he mentioned it."
"7771","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, and from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to seclude himself in the last ten days of Ramadan until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, took him."
"7772","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I am ruined, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And what is that? He said: I had intercourse with my wife in Ramadan. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Can you find a slave to free? He said: No. He said: Are you able to fast two consecutive months? He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Can you not feed sixty poor persons? He said: I cannot find it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a basket - and the basket is a large receptacle - containing dates. He said: Go and give it in charity. He said: To one poorer than me? By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava fields more in need of it than us. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed, then said: Take it to your family."
"7773","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not fast continuously. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously. He said: I am not like you; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink. He said: They did not stop continuous fasting, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fasted continuously with them for two days and two nights. Then they saw the crescent. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had the crescent been delayed, I would have added more for you, as one rebuking them."
"7774","Abdallah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us - and Abd al-Ala from Ma'mar - from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to encourage standing in Ramadan without commanding them firmly, saying: Whoever stands in Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his past sins will be forgiven."
"7775","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us - and Abd al-Ala from Ma'mar - from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Every deed of the son of Adam is his except fasting. Fasting is Mine, and I shall reward for it. The changed breath of the mouth of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"7776","Al-Zuhri said: And Said ibn al-Musayyab informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, when he was taken by night: I met Musa, peace be upon him, and he described him. He said: A man - I think he said - lean, lank-haired, as though from the men of Shanuah. He said: And I met Isa, peace be upon him, and he described him, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Of medium stature, reddish, as though just brought out of a bath - meaning a hammam. He said: And I saw Ibrahim, peace be upon him, and I am the most resembling of his children to him. He said: Then I was brought two vessels, one containing milk and the other containing wine. It was said to me: Take whichever of them you wish. So I took the milk and drank it. It was said to me: You have been guided to the natural disposition, and you have attained the natural disposition. Had you taken the wine, your nation would have gone astray."
"7777","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Hisham ibn Hassan narrating from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: I was with Abu Hurayrah when a man asked him about something I did not know what it was. He said: Abu Hurayrah said: Allah is Greatest; two asked about it, and this is the third. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Men will be carried by questioning to excess until they say: Allah created creation, so who created Him?"
"7778","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"7779","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, descends every night when the first third of the night has passed, saying: I am the King. Who is it that asks Me, that I may give him? Who is it that calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Who is it that seeks My forgiveness, that I may forgive him? He remains thus until dawn."
"7780","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar said, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I seek the forgiveness of Allah in a day more than seventy times, and I repent to Him."
"7781","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to the prayer, let him come with dignity and calm. Let him pray what he catches, and make up what he missed."
"7782","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Habib, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every child is born upon the natural disposition. Then his parents make him Jewish and make him Christian, like cattle brought forth whole, whose ears are then slit."
"7783","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to me, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be trials; the one sitting in them is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, the one walking is better than the one hastening. Whoever finds a refuge or a shelter, let him seek refuge in it."
"7784","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: There will be a trial; he did not attribute it to the Prophet. He said: Whoever finds a refuge or a shelter, let him seek refuge in it."
"7785","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever catches a rakah of Asr before the sun sets has caught it. That is narrated from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. And whoever catches a rakah of Fajr before the sun rises has caught it."
"7786","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, Ubaydallah ibn Abdallah ibn Utbah informed me that Abu Hurayrah said: A Bedouin stood and urinated in the mosque, so the people seized him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Leave him, and pour over his urine a bucket of water, or a water-skin of water. You were sent as facilitators, and you were not sent as hardship-makers."
"7787","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, Ubaydallah ibn Abdallah narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah informed him that a Bedouin urinated in the mosque, and he mentioned its meaning."
"7788","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Every step he takes toward the prayer, a good deed is written for him by it, and a bad deed is erased from him by it."
"7789","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rose for prayer, and we rose with him. A Bedouin said while in prayer: O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and have mercy on no one with us. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished, he said to the Bedouin: You have confined what is vast - meaning the mercy of Allah."
"7790","Ibrahim narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, who said: Satan comes to one of you in his prayer, so he does not know whether he added or decreased. When one of you finds that, let him prostrate two prostrations."
"7791","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Rabah, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Salamah informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The prayer was established and the people arranged their rows for prayer. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us from his house, walking until he stood in his place of prayer. Then he remembered that he had not taken a bath. So he said to the people: Stay in your place. He returned to his house. He said: Then he came out to us while we were in rows, and stood in prayer with his head dripping, having taken a bath."
"7792","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Muhammad ibn Ziyad from Abu Hurayrah - that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the servant of one of you brings him his food, having endured its heat, its hardship, its smoke, and its burden, let him seat him with him. If he refuses, let him hand him a morsel in his hand."
"7793","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from a man of Banu Ghifar, that he heard Said al-Maqburi narrating from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The grateful eater is like the patient fasting person."
"7794","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, invoked blessing upon the predawn meal and upon tharid."
"7795","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from a man, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had the one who drinks while standing known what is in his belly, he would have vomited it."
"7796","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, the like of the hadith of al-Zuhri."
"7797","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you rises from his seat, then returns to it, he has the most right to it."
"7798","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ubaydallah ibn Umar, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you rises at night, then returns to his bed, let him shake his bedding with the inner side of his waist-wrapper, for he does not know what came after him. Then let him say: In Your name, O Allah, I lay my side, and in Your name I raise it. O Allah, if You take my soul, forgive it, and if You send it back, guard it with that by which You guard the righteous."
"7799","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he removes them, let him begin with the left. Let him remove them both together, and wear them both together."
"7800","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Five are of the natural disposition: shaving the pubes, circumcision, trimming the mustache, plucking the armpit, and clipping the nails."
"7801","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer is like the example of a crop: the wind keeps bending it, and the believer keeps being struck by affliction; and the example of the hypocrite is like the example of the cedar tree, which does not shake until it is harvested."
"7802","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes up, let him not put his hand into his vessel - or he said: into his ablution water - until he has washed it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"7803","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: I saw Abu Hurayrah pass by people performing ablution from a purification vessel, and he said: Perform ablution well, may Allah have mercy on you. Have you not heard what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"7804","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir - as I think he said - from Damdam, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to kill the two black ones in prayer: the scorpion and the snake. And Abd al-Razzaq said: Thus he narrated to us innumerable times."
"7805","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar and al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor and the caller to prayer is trusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers to prayer."
"7806","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: I heard Ibn Ukaymah narrating from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer in which he recited aloud, then turned to the people after he gave the salutation and said: Did any one of you recite with me just now? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I say, what is wrong with me that the Quran is being contested with me? So the people stopped reciting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in that in which he recites aloud, when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7807","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr or Asr and gave the salutation after two rakahs, then left. The hasty people went out and said: The prayer has been shortened. Dhu al-Shimalayn said: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying? They said: He is right. So he prayed with them the two rakahs he had left, then prostrated two prostrations while sitting after he gave the salutation."
"7808","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not make your houses graves, for Satan flees from the house in which Surat al-Baqarah is recited."
"7809","Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar and Abd al-Ala informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you and confuses him in his prayer, so he does not know whether he added or decreased. If one of you finds that, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"7810","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri - Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me - from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed on Friday there is an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with while asking Allah for something therein except that He gives it to him."
"7811","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed on Friday there is an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with while asking Allah for something therein except that He gives it to him."
"7812","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the incoming caravans; whoever meets them and buys, then its owner has the choice when he reaches the market."
"7813","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri - Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab informed me - that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: May Allah destroy the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"7814","Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Ja'far - meaning Ibn Burqan - narrated to us, who said: I heard Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at your forms and your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds."
"7815","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The wound caused by a stray beast is without liability, and the well is without liability, and the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"7816","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the heat intensifies, cool down with the prayer, for intense heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"7817","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from the hadith of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Does a man pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you have two garments?"
"7818","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - and Abd al-Razzaq did not raise it to the Prophet: May Allah destroy the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"7819","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us - and Abd al-Razzaq in his hadith said: Ibn Shihab informed me - from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not listened to anything as He has listened to one who - Abd al-Razzaq said: to one who chants the Quran. A companion of his said, adding: in that which he recites aloud."
"7820","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ibn Shihab informed me, who said: I heard Ibn Ukaymah saying: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in a prayer in which he recited aloud, then gave the salutation and turned to the people and said: Did anyone recite with me just now? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I say, what is wrong with me that the Quran is being contested with me?"
"7821","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah informing them, saying: In every prayer there is recitation. What the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us, we make audible to you, and what he concealed from us, we conceal from you."
"7822","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari said, al-Awza'i said, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed are those who took the graves of their prophets as mosques."
"7823","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub informed me that Abu al-Sa'ib, the freed slave of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Quran, it is defective, it is defective, incomplete. Abu al-Sa'ib said to Abu Hurayrah: I am sometimes behind the imam. Abu al-Sa'ib said: So Abu Hurayrah nudged my arm and said: O Persian, recite it to yourself, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I have divided the prayer between Me and My servant into two halves; half of it is for Me and half of it is for My servant, and for My servant is what he asks. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite. The servant says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Then Allah says: My servant has praised Me. And the servant says: The Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Then Allah says: My servant has extolled Me. And the servant says: Master of the Day of Judgment. Then Allah says: My servant has glorified Me - and He said: This is between Me and My servant. The servant says: You alone we worship and You alone we ask for help. He said: I find it for My servant, and for My servant is what he asks. He said: My servant says: Guide us to the straight path, the path of those You have blessed, not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: This is for My servant [source text ends here truncated: and for My servant]."
"7824","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated, from Ibn Jurayj, each of them said - each of them the freed slave of Abd Allah ibn Hisham ibn Zuhrah - and they said Malik, and Ibn Bakr said: Abu Hurayrah says: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite. The servant stands and says [source text ends here truncated]."
"7825","He said: And Yaqub narrated it to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub, the freed slave of al-Huraqah, narrated to me, from Abu al-Sa'ib, the freed slave of Abd Allah ibn Zuhrah al-Taymi, from Abu Hurayrah, and he mentioned the hadith."
"7826","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah - Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Qari informed him - that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: By the Lord of this House, I did not forbid fasting on Friday, but Muhammad forbade it. By the Lord of this House, I did not say: Whoever is overtaken by dawn while in a state of major impurity should break his fast, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it. Abd al-Razzaq in his hadith said: Yahya ibn Ja'dah informed him - Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Qari - that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying."
"7827","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Isra'il informed us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the fasting day of one of you, let him not utter obscenity nor act ignorantly; if someone acts ignorantly toward him, let him say: I am a fasting man."
"7828","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man removed a thorny branch from the path of the Muslims and he was forgiven. Abdullah said: This hadith is raised to the Prophet, but Sufyan fell short in raising it."
"7829","Sufyan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah: A man proposed to a woman, and he - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - said: Look at her, for in the eyes of the Ansar there is something."
"7830","Hammad ibn Usamah Abu Usamah narrated to us, who said: Ubayd Allah informed me, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar marriage."
"7831","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has made sacred by my tongue what is between the two lava plains of Madinah. Then he came to Banu Harithah and said: O Banu Harithah, I see you have gone out of the sanctuary. Then he looked and said: Rather you are in it, rather you are in it."
"7832","Hammad ibn Usamah informed us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Qays, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said on the way some poetry: O night, for your length and your toil, yet you have saved me from the land of disbelief. He said: And a slave boy of mine ran away from me on the way. He said: When I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him, while I was with him, the boy appeared. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Hurayrah, this is your boy. I said: He is for the sake of Allah, and I freed him."
"7833","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed faith retreats to Madinah as the snake retreats to its hole."
"7834","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman was punished for a cat she kept until it died of hunger; she did not feed it nor let it go to eat from the vermin of the earth. And a man was forgiven for removing a thorny branch from the path."
"7835","Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr al-Laythi narrated to me, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputing about the Quran is disbelief."
"7836","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid - meaning Isma'il - narrated to me, from Abu Malik al-Aslami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away Ma'iz ibn Malik three times; when he came the fourth time, he ordered him to be stoned."
"7837","Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, the like of it."
"7838","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of slavewomen."
"7839","Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to a gathering, let him greet with peace; if it occurs to him to sit, then when he stands, let him greet with peace; the first is not more obligatory than the last."
"7840","Abdah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were not to impose hardship on my community, I would command them to use the tooth-stick at every prayer."
"7841","And he said - meaning Abdah - Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, the like of it."
"7842","Ayyub ibn al-Najjar Abu Isma'il al-Yamami narrated to us, from Tayyib ibn Muhammad, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the effeminate men who imitate women, and the masculine women who imitate men, and one who rides the open land alone."
"7843","Ayyub ibn al-Najjar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam disputed with Musa. He said: O Adam, you are the one who brought people out of Paradise by your sin and made them wretched. Adam said to him: You are the one whom Allah chose over people with His messages and His speech, yet you blame me for a matter which Allah decreed for me before He created me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So Adam overcame Musa."
"7844","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Yahya - meaning Ibn Abi Kathir - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Yaqub - or Ibn Yaqub - from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the believer is to the muscle of his shins, then to half his shins, then to his ankles; what is below that is in the Fire."
"7845","Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false speech. Do not spy, do not eavesdrop, do not compete with one another, do not artificially inflate prices against one another, do not turn away from one another, do not hate one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers."
"7846","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Affliction continues with the believer, man or woman, in his body, his wealth, and his child, until he meets Allah with no sin upon him."
"7847","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A funeral was brought past the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Stand up, for death is a fright."
"7848","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family; whoever leaves helpless dependents, then to me."
"7849","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man lying on his stomach and said: This is a lying position which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not love."
"7850","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which deeds are best and which deeds are good? He said: Faith in Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then which, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Striving in the path of Allah, the peak of deeds. He said: Then which, O Messenger of Allah? He said: An accepted pilgrimage."
"7851","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the crescent and said: When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break your fast; if it is obscured from you, count thirty."
"7852","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi Salih al-Samman narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one endures the hardship of Madinah and its strain except that I will be for him an intercessor and a witness - or: a witness and an intercessor."
"7853","My father said: Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, doubting about it: a witness or an intercessor."
"7854","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to me that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"7855","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed us, who said: I heard Abu Maryam mentioning, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating in stagnant water and then performing ablution from it."
"7856","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hilal al-Qurashi informed me, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque. When he stood, we stood with him. A Bedouin came to him and said: Give me, O Muhammad. He said: No, and I seek Allah's forgiveness. He pulled him and scratched him. He said: They rushed at him. He said: Leave him. He said: Then he gave him. His oath was to say: No, and I seek Allah's forgiveness."
"7857","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from four: from the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, the trial of life and death, and the trial of the Dajjal."
"7858","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Malik ibn Zal im, from Abu Hurayrah, that he narrated to Marwan ibn al-Hakam, saying: My beloved Abu al-Qasim, the truthful, the believed (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me: The destruction of my community is at the hands of foolish youths from Quraysh."
"7859","Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan, I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah saying: I do not know how many times I saw Abu Hurayrah standing in the market saying: Knowledge will be taken away, trials will appear, and harj will increase. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is harj? He said with his hand like this, and he turned it."
"7860","Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days; what is beyond that is charity."
"7861","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For a man's belly to be filled with pus that oozes is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"7862","Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Nabhan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another, do not artificially inflate prices against one another, do not envy one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers."
"7863","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me - meaning Hasan and Husayn."
"7864","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl al-Hashimi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he performed ablution washing twice."
"7865","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe. They said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his evils. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are his evils? He said: His evil."
"7866","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ajlan, the freed slave of al-Mushma'ill, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every newborn of the children of Adam is touched by Satan with his finger, except Maryam daughter of Imran and her son Isa, peace be upon them."
"7867","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, a man from Quraysh narrated to me, from his father, that he was with Abu Hurayrah, and Abu Hurayrah saw a horse made of rags in a slave girl's hand and said: Do you not see this? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only one who has no share on the Day of Resurrection makes this."
"7868","Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) encouraging people to stand in prayer in Ramadan, saying: Whoever stands it in faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not gather the people for the standing."
"7869","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A tribe of Banu Isra'il was lost, and he mentioned the mouse, and said: Do you not see that if you bring camel's milk near it, it does not approach it, and if you bring sheep's milk to it, it drinks it? He said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Do I recite the Torah?"
"7870","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, who said: Abu Hurayrah was asked: Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Omen is in three: in the dwelling, the horse, and the woman? He said: I said: Then I would be saying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say; but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The truest of omens is the good omen, and the evil eye is real."
"7871","Rawh narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar informed us, I heard Abu al-Ghadiyah al-Yamami saying: I came to Madinah, and the messenger of Kathir ibn al-Salt came and invited them, and none stood except Abu Hurayrah and five of them, I being one of them. They went and ate, then Abu Hurayrah came and washed his hand, then said: By Allah, O people of the mosque, you are disobedient to Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7872","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the Negus and magnified over him four times."
"7873","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sayhan and Jayhan and the Nile and the Euphrates, each is from the rivers of Paradise."
"7874","Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophet nor caliph - or he said: There is no prophet except that he has two confidants: a confidant commanding him to good and forbidding him evil, and a confidant who does not spare him ruin. Whoever is protected from the evil of the bad confidant has been protected. He says it three times, and he is with the one that prevails over him of the two."
"7875","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he sniffed water into his nose, he put the water into his nostrils."
"7876","Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Hurrah narrated to me, from his uncle Hakim ibn Abi Hurrah, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said - I do not know it except from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The grateful eater has like that of the patient fasting person."
"7877","Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Salman al-Agharr, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a double-faced person to be trustworthy."
"7878","Ayyub ibn al-Najjar narrated to us, from Tayyib ibn Muhammad, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the effeminate men who imitate women, and the masculine women who imitate men, and the celibate men who say: We will not marry, and the celibate women who say that, and one who rides the open land alone. It weighed heavily on the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until it became evident in their faces. And he said: One who spends the night alone."
"7879","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Budhawayh informed me, one who heard Wahb saying informed me - meaning Hammam, thus my father said - Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you remains in prayer as long as he waits for the next one, and the angels keep praying for one of you as long as he is in his mosque, saying: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him, as long as he does not break ablution. A man from Hadramawt said: What is that breaking, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: Indeed Allah is not shy of the truth: if he passes wind audibly or silently."
"7880","Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan informed us: He sought permission from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd while he was praying, and he glorified for me. When he gave the salutation, he said: The permission of a man when in prayer is to glorify, and the permission of a woman is to clap."
"7881","Marwan narrated to us, Awf informed us, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet, the like of it."
"7882","Marwan narrated to us, Awf informed me, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, the like of it."
"7883","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Odd and loves the odd."
"7884","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Resting the hands on the hips in prayer was forbidden. We said to Hisham: What is resting on the hips? He said: He puts his hand on his waist while praying. Yazid said: We said to Hisham: Did he mention it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said with his head: Yes."
"7885","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the evening three times: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, no venom will harm him that night. He said: Our family had learned it and used to say it. A slave girl of them was stung and felt no pain from it."
"7886","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended a funeral, he asked: Is there debt on your companion? If they said: Yes, he said: Does he have means to repay it? If they said: Yes, he prayed over him; if they said: No, he said: Pray over your companion. When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, opened the conquests to him, he said: I am closer to the believers than themselves; whoever leaves debt, it is upon me, and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."
"7887","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Abbas, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Ibn Mikraz, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man wants to strive in the path of Allah while seeking worldly gain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no reward for him. The people deemed that grave and said to the man: Go back to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); perhaps he did not understand. He went back and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man wants to strive in the path of Allah while seeking worldly gain. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no reward for him. Then he went back the third time, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no reward for him."
"7888","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad - meaning Ibn Amr - informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah ibn Nawfal, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer in which the Mother of the Quran is not recited is defective, then defective."
"7889","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan - meaning Ibn Husayn - informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Hakim al-Dabbi, who said: Abu Hurayrah said to me: When you come to the people of your city, inform them that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The first thing of which the servant will be judged on the Day of Resurrection is his prescribed prayer. If it is sound - and Yazid once said: If he completed it - otherwise it will be supplemented from his voluntary prayers. Then the same will be done with the rest of the obligatory deeds."
"7890","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Hanzalah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Isa son of Maryam will descend and kill the pig, erase the cross, prayer will be gathered for him, wealth will be given until it is not accepted, tribute will be abolished, and he will descend at al-Rawha and perform pilgrimage from it, or lesser pilgrimage, or both. He said: And Abu Hurayrah recited: And there is none of the People of the Book except that he will believe in him before his death, and on the Day of Resurrection he will be a witness over them. Hanzalah claimed that Abu Hurayrah said: He believes in him before his death - Isa. I do not know whether all this is the hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or something Abu Hurayrah said."
"7891","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh, the Ansar, Juhaynah, Muzaynah, Aslam, Ghifar, and Ashja' are my allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger."
"7892","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us - and Abu al-Nadr said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us - the meaning - from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came out to you with the Night of Decree clarified to me, and the false messiah. There was a dispute between two men at the entrance of the mosque, so I came to them to separate them, and both were made forgotten to me. I will give you a hint of them: As for the Night of Decree, seek it in the last ten, odd. As for the false messiah, he is blind in the eye, prominent in the forehead, wide in the neck, in him is crookedness, as if he is Qatan ibn Abd al-Uzza. He said: O Messenger of Allah, will his resemblance harm me? He said: No, you are a Muslim man and he is a disbelieving man."
"7893","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Awn, from his brother Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a black non-Arab slave girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I must free a believing slave. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Where is Allah? She pointed to the sky with her forefinger. He said to her: Who am I? She pointed with her finger to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and to the sky: That you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her."
"7894","Yazid narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Dawud ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about what most causes people to enter the Fire. He said: The two hollows: the mouth and the private part. And he was asked about what most causes entry to Paradise. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good character."
"7895","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abu al-Rabi', from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are from the affairs of ignorance which people will not leave: disparaging lineages, wailing over the dead, seeking rain by the stars, and: a mangy camel infects a hundred - who infected the first camel?"
"7896","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad - meaning Ibn Ishaq - informed us, from Salih ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call the grapevine al-karm, for al-karm is only the believing man."
"7897","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Sa'id ibn Sam'an, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah informing Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pledge will be given to a man between the Corner and the Maqam. Only its people will violate the sanctity of the House; when they violate it, do not ask about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Abyssinians will come and destroy it, a destruction after which it will never be inhabited, and they are those who will extract its treasure."
"7898","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he drinks intoxicant, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck. Al-Zuhri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drunk man a fourth time and he let him go."
"7899","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah informed us, Ishaq ibn Bakr ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deceptive years will come over people: the liar will be believed therein, the truthful will be disbelieved therein, the treacherous will be trusted therein, the trustworthy will be accused of treachery therein, and al-Ruwaybidah will speak therein. It was said: What is al-Ruwaybidah? He said: The fool speaks about public affairs."
"7900","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi informed us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Abu al-Rabi', from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, forgive me what I did before and after, what I concealed and declared, and my excess, and what You know better than me. You are the Advancer and the Delayer; there is no god but You."
"7901","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, that Abu Hurayrah said when death came to him: Do not pitch a tent over me, nor follow me with a censer, and hasten with me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the righteous man is placed upon his bier he says: Take me forward, take me forward, and when the evil man is placed upon his bier he says: Woe to him, where are you taking me."
"7902","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn of the sons of Adam is touched by Satan with his finger, except Maryam and her son, upon them be peace."
"7903","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Men from around the mosque who do not attend the last Isha in congregation will surely desist, or I shall surely burn around their houses with bundles of firewood."
"7904","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Hisham informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Aswad, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation has been given five traits in Ramadan which no nation before them was given: the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk, and the angels seek forgiveness for them until they break fast, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic adorns His Paradise every day then says: My righteous servants are about to cast off from themselves burden and harm and come to you, and in it the rebellious devils are chained so they do not reach what they used to reach in other than it, and they are forgiven in the last night. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, is it the Night of Decree. He said: No, but the worker is only paid his wage when he completes his work."
"7905","Yazid narrated to us, Abu Mashar informed us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that a Bedouin gave a young camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he compensated him with six young camels, but he was displeased. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: So-and-so gave me a she-camel as a gift, and it is my she-camel, I know it as I know some of my family, it went away from me on the day of Zaghabaat, so I compensated him with six young camels, yet he remained displeased. I was about to accept a gift only from a Qurashi, or an Ansari, or a Thaqafi, or a Dawsi."
"7906","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man went out visiting a brother of his for the sake of Allah the Mighty and Majestic in another village, so Allah the Mighty and Majestic stationed an angel on his path, and when he passed by him he said: Where do you intend. He said: I intend so-and-so. He said: For kinship. He said: No. He said: For a favor of his with you which you maintain. He said: No. He said: Then why do you come to him. He said: I love him for Allah. He said: Then I am the messenger of Allah to you, that He loves you for your love of him for His sake."
"7907","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Farqad, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The most lying of people, or among the most lying of people, are the goldsmiths and the dyers."
"7908","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever Allah gives something of this wealth without his asking for it, let him accept it, for it is only provision which Allah the Mighty and Majestic has driven to him."
"7909","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd Allah ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: Whoever closes his door is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abu Sufyan is safe."
"7910","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Paradise is one hundred degrees, between every two degrees is one hundred years."
"7911","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the servant obeys his Lord and his master, he has two rewards."
"7912","Yazid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Increase remembrance of the destroyer of pleasures. My father said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, he is Abu Bani Shaybah. Yazid narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Amr with ninety-nine hadiths, then he completed them with this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), completing one hundred hadiths."
"7913","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah al-Jumahi informed us, from Ishaq ibn Bakr ibn Abi al-Furat, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The hypocrites have signs by which they are known: their greeting is cursing, and their food is plunder, and their booty is misappropriation, and they do not approach the mosques except forsaking them, and they do not come to prayer except at the end, arrogant, they do not befriend nor are they befriended, logs by night, noisy by day. And Yazid once said: loud by day."
"7914","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah. My father said, and Abu Kamil said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, Ata ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, to the same meaning, that the people said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, will we see our Lord the Mighty and Majestic on the Day of Resurrection. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you suffer harm in seeing the moon on the night of full moon. They said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you suffer harm in seeing the sun with no cloud beneath it. They said: No. He said: Then you will see Him likewise. Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. So whoever worshipped the sun will follow the sun, and whoever worshipped the moon will follow the moon, and whoever worshipped false deities will follow false deities, and this nation will remain, with its intercessors or its hypocrites, Abu Kamil said: Ibrahim doubted. Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic will come to them in a form other than His form which they know, and will say: I am your Lord. So they will say: We seek refuge with Allah from you, this is our place until our Lord comes to us, and when our Lord comes we will know Him. Then Allah the Mighty and Majestic will come to them in His form which they know, and will say: I am your Lord. So they will say: You are our Lord, and they will follow Him. And the bridge will be struck across the midst of Hell, and I and my nation will be the first to cross, and none will speak that day except the messengers, and the supplication of the messengers that day is: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. And in Hell are hooks like the thorns of al-Sadan. Have you seen al-Sadan. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They are like the thorns of al-Sadan, except that none knows the measure of their greatness but Allah the Exalted. They snatch people by their deeds, so among them is one destroyed by his deed, or he said: bound by his deed, or scratched, and among them is one recompensed, Abu Kamil said in his hadith: Ibrahim doubted, and among them is scratched or recompensed. Then He will manifest, until when Allah the Mighty and Majestic finishes judging between the servants and intends by His mercy to bring out of the people of the Fire whoever says: There is no god but Allah, He will command the angels to bring out of the Fire whoever did not associate anything with Allah among those whom Allah intends to mercy among those who say: There is no god but Allah. So they will know them in the Fire, they will know them by the mark of prostration. The Fire eats the son of Adam except the mark of prostration, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic has forbidden the Fire to eat the mark of prostration. So they will come out of the Fire having been scorched, and the water of life will be poured upon them, and they will sprout as the grain sprouts, and Abu Kamil said: the grain also, in the flood-borne debris. And a man will remain with his face turned toward the Fire, and he is the last of the people of Paradise to enter, and he will say: O Lord, turn my face away from the Fire, for its wind has poisoned me and its smoke has burned me. So he will supplicate Allah as long as He wills him to supplicate, then Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say: Perhaps if that is done for you, you will ask for other than it. So he will say: No, by Your might, I will not ask for other than it. And he will give his Lord the Mighty and Majestic covenants and pledges as He wills. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic will turn his face away from the Fire. Then when he faces Paradise and sees it, he will be silent as long as Allah wills him to be silent, then he will say: O Lord, bring me near to the gate of Paradise. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say to him: Did you not give your covenants and pledges that you would not ask Me for other than what I gave you. Woe to you, O son of Adam, how treacherous you are. So he will say: O Lord. And he will supplicate Allah until He says to him: Then perhaps if that is given you, you will ask for other than it. So he will say: No, by Your might, I will not ask for other than it. So he will give his Lord the Mighty and Majestic whatever He wills of covenants and pledges. So He will bring him forward to the gate of Paradise. Then when he stands at the gate of Paradise, Paradise will open wide for him, and he will see what is in it of bliss and joy. So he will be silent as long as Allah wills him to be silent, then he will say: O Lord, admit me to Paradise. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say to him: Did you not give your covenants and pledges that you would not ask Me for other than what I gave you. Woe to you, O son of Adam, how treacherous you are. So he will say: O Lord, let me not be the most wretched of Your creation. So he will keep supplicating Allah until Allah laughs at him. Then when Allah the Mighty and Majestic laughs at him, He will say: Enter Paradise. Then when he enters it, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say to him: Wish. So he will ask his Lord the Mighty and Majestic and wish, until Allah the Mighty and Majestic will even remind him, saying: Of such and such. Until when his hopes are cut off, Allah the Mighty and Majestic will say to him: For you is that and the like of it with it. Ata ibn Yazid said: And Abu Said al-Khudri was with Abu Hurayrah, not rejecting anything of his hadith, until when Abu Hurayrah narrated that Allah the Mighty and Majestic said to that man: and the like of it with it, Abu Said said: And ten times its like with it, O Abu Hurayrah. Abu Hurayrah said: I memorized only His saying: That is for you and the like of it with it. Abu Said said: I bear witness that I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) his saying about that man: For you is ten times its like. Abu Hurayrah said: And that man is the last of the people of Paradise to enter."
"7915","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, from al-Zuhri, and Yaqub said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab. My father said: And this is the hadith of Sulayman al-Hashimi, from Amr ibn Usayd ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi, ally of Banu Zuhrah, and he was among the companions of Abu Hurayrah, that Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ten men as scouts and put in command over them Asim ibn Thabit ibn Abi al-Aqlah, grandfather of Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab. They went until when they were at al-Hadah between Usfan and Makkah, they were reported to a clan of Hudhayl called Banu Lihyan. So they rushed toward them with nearly one hundred archers, and they tracked their traces until they found their eating of dates in a dwelling where they had stopped. They said: Date pits of Yathrib. So they followed their traces. When Asim and his companions were told of them, they took refuge on a hill. The people surrounded them and said to them: Come down and give us your hands, and for you is the covenant and pledge that we will not kill anyone of you. Asim ibn Thabit, commander of the people, said: As for me, by Allah, I will not come down under the protection of a disbeliever. O Allah, inform our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about us. So they shot them with arrows and killed Asim among seven. And three men came down to them upon the covenant and pledge, among them Khubayb al-Ansari, and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah, and another man. When they got hold of them, they loosened the strings of their bows and tied them with them. The third man said: This is the first treachery. By Allah, I will not accompany you. I have in these an example, meaning death. So they dragged him and struggled with him, but he refused to accompany them, so they killed him. They went off with Khubayb and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah until they sold them in Makkah after the battle of Badr. The sons of al-Harith ibn Amir ibn Nawfal ibn Abd Manaf bought Khubayb, and Khubayb was the one who killed al-Harith ibn Amir ibn Nawfal on the day of Badr. Khubayb remained with them as a captive until they agreed to kill him. He borrowed from one of the daughters of al-Harith a razor to shave with for the killing, so she lent it to him. A little son of hers crawled, she said, while I was heedless, until he came to him, and she found him seating him on his thigh with the razor in his hand. She said: So I was frightened with a fright which Khubayb recognized. He said: Do you fear that I will kill him. I would not do that. She said: By Allah, I never saw a captive better than Khubayb. She said: By Allah, I found him one day eating a bunch of grapes in his hand while he was bound in iron, and there was no fruit in Makkah. And she used to say: It is provision which Allah provided Khubayb. When they took him out of the sanctuary to kill him in the lawful area, Khubayb said to them: Let me bow two rakahs. So they left him, and he bowed two rakahs, then said: By Allah, were it not that you think that what is with me is panic from death, I would have added. O Allah, count them in number, and kill them piecemeal, and leave none of them. I do not care when I am killed as a Muslim, on whichever side my death for Allah is, and that is for the sake of God, and if He wills He blesses upon the joints of a dismembered corpse. Then Abu Sirwaah Uqbah ibn al-Harith stood to him and killed him. And Khubayb was the one who established prayer for every Muslim killed in captivity. And Allah the Mighty and Majestic answered Asim ibn Thabit on the day he was struck, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed his companions on the day they were struck of their news. And some people of Quraysh sent to Asim ibn Thabit when they were told he was killed, to be brought something of him by which he would be known, and he had killed a man of their great ones on the day of Badr. So Allah the Mighty and Majestic sent upon Asim a canopy-like cloud of hornets, and it protected him from their messengers, and they could not cut anything from him."
"7916","Yazid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Awn informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd Abu Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a funeral, walking, and when I walked he outpaced me, so I hurried and outpaced him. A man beside me turned and said: The earth is folded for him, by the Friend of Ibrahim."
"7917","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Placing the hands on the flanks in prayer was forbidden. So we said to Hisham: Did he mention it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said with his head, meaning yes."
"7918","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Kinship is a branch from the Most Merciful the Mighty and Majestic. It will come on the Day of Resurrection saying: O Lord, I was severed. O Lord, I was wronged. O Lord, I was ill-treated."
"7919","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Maymunah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when I see you my soul is pleased and my eye is delighted, so inform me about everything. So he said: Everything was created from water. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about a deed which if I hold to it I will enter Paradise. He said: Spread peace, and feed food, and join kinship, and stand at night while people are asleep, then enter Paradise in peace."
"7920","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, beardless, white, curly-haired, kohled, sons of thirty-three, upon the creation of Adam, sixty cubits tall in a width of seven cubits."
"7921","Yazid and Abu Kamil said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Isl ibn Sufyan, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade letting garments hang down in prayer."
"7922","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Souls are enlisted troops: those of them which recognize one another unite, and those which do not recognize one another differ."
"7923","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever has two wives and inclines to one of them over the other will come on the Day of Resurrection dragging one of his sides fallen or inclined. Yazid doubted."
"7924","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, and Affan: Hammad narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Aws ibn Khalid, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Beast will emerge, and with it the staff of Musa, upon him be peace, and the seal of Sulayman, upon him be peace. So it will brand the nose of the disbeliever, Affan said: the nose of the disbeliever, with the seal, and will brighten the face of the believer with the staff, until the people at the tables gather upon their tables, and this one will say: O believer, and this one will say: O disbeliever."
"7925","Yazid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Umar informed us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you goes to his bed, let him shake it with the inner part of his waist-wrapper, for he does not know what happened after him. And when he lays his side, let him say: In Your name, O Allah, I lay my side, and by You I raise it. O Allah, if You withhold my soul, forgive it, and if You send it back, guard it with what You guard Your righteous servants."
"7926","Yazid narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Muslim informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank people."
"7927","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah the Mighty and Majestic looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"7928","Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun informed us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd ibn Umayr al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: While a man was in a desert land, he heard a voice in a cloud: Water the garden of so-and-so. So that cloud moved aside and emptied its water in a lava field. He went to the lava field, and there it was in the ends of watercourses, and a watercourse among those watercourses had taken all that water. So he followed the water, and there was a man standing in his garden turning the water with his spade. So he said to him: O servant of Allah, what is your name. He said: So-and-so, with the name which he heard in the cloud. So he said to him: O servant of Allah, why do you ask me about my name. He said: I heard a voice in the cloud whose water this is saying: Water the garden of so-and-so, for your name. So what do you do in it. He said: Since you said this, I look at what comes out of it, so I give a third of it in charity, and I and my family eat a third of it, and I return a third of it into it."
"7929","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever covers his Muslim brother in this world, Allah will cover him in the Hereafter, and whoever relieves his brother of a distress among the distresses of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah is in the aid of the servant as long as the servant is in the aid of his brother."
"7930","Yazid narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire."
"7931","Yazid narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Qays ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves obedience and parts the community and dies, his death is a death of ignorance. And whoever fights under a blind banner, angered for his partisanship, and fighting for his partisanship, and supporting his partisanship, and is killed, his killing is a killing of ignorance. And whoever goes out against my nation striking its righteous and its wicked, not sparing its believer nor fulfilling toward its covenanted, he is not from me and I am not from him."
"7932","Yazid narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, who said: I came to Abu Hurayrah and said to him: It reached me that you say a good deed is multiplied a thousand thousand good deeds. He said: What amazes you of that. By Allah, I heard him, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my father said likewise, say: Allah multiplies the good deed two thousand thousand good deeds."
"7933","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor of the believers will enter Paradise before their rich by five hundred years."
"7934","Yazid narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zakariyya, upon him be peace, was a carpenter."
"7935","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man committed a sin and said: Lord, I committed a sin, or he said: I did a deed, a sin, so forgive it. So He the Mighty and Majestic said: My servant did a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and seizes for it. I have forgiven My servant. Then he did another sin, or committed another sin, and said: Lord, I did a sin, so forgive it. So He the Blessed and Exalted said: My servant knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and seizes for it. I have forgiven My servant. Then he did another sin, or committed another sin, and said: Lord, I did a sin, so forgive it. So He said: My servant knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and seizes for it. I have forgiven My servant, so let him do what he wishes."
"7936","Muhammad and Husayn said: Awf narrated to us, from Abu Qahdham, who said: There was found in the time of Ziyad, or Ibn Ziyad, a purse with grain like date pits, upon it was written: This grew in a time when justice was practiced."
"7937","Ishaq ibn Yusuf, and he is al-Azraq, narrated to us, Awf informed us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If knowledge were at the Pleiades, men from the sons of Faris would reach it."
"7938","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into the Fire and found most of its people were women, and I looked into Paradise and saw most of its people were the poor."
"7939","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan informed us, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the believer sins, there is a black dot in his heart. If he repents and desists and seeks forgiveness, his heart is polished. And if he increases, it increases until it covers his heart. That is the rust which Allah the Mighty and Majestic mentioned in the Quran: Nay, but rust has covered their hearts for what they earned."
"7940","Safwan narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan informed us, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyr feels of the touch of killing only as one of you feels the touch of a pinch."
"7941","Safwan narrated to me, Ibn Ajlan informed us, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere advice, three times. He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, to whom. He said: To Allah, and to His Book, and to the leaders of the Muslims."
"7942","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Hilal ibn Abi Zaynab, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: The martyr was mentioned with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The earth does not dry of the blood of the martyr until his two wives hasten to him as though they are two foster mothers who lost, or misplaced, their two young ones in an open land. In the hand of each of them is a garment better than this world and what is in it."
"7943","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good opinion is part of good worship."
"7944","Safwan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan informed us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, which people are best. He said: I and those with me. So it was said to him: Then who, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The one upon the trail. It was said to him: Then who, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then he dismissed them."
"7945","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Isa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man speaks a word intending no harm by it, and falls with it seventy autumns into the Fire."
"7946","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, of the family of Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrating from Ubayd, freedman of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayrah, that he met a woman and found from her the scent of a strong gust of perfume. So Abu Hurayrah said to her: Do you intend the mosque. She said: Yes. He said: And did you perfume yourself for it. She said: Yes. Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No woman perfumes herself for the mosque and Allah accepts a prayer for her until she washes from it as she washes from janabah. So go and wash."
"7947","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Furat, I heard Abu Hazim say: I sat with Abu Hurayrah five years, and I heard him narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The Children of Israil were ruled by the prophets: whenever a prophet perished, a prophet succeeded him. And there is no prophet after me. There will be caliphs and they will be many. They said: Then what do you command us. He said: Fulfill the pledge of the first, then the first, and give them their right which Allah made for them, for Allah will ask them about what He entrusted to them."
"7948","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, who said: I heard Amr ibn Asim narrating that he heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Inform me of something I say when I wake and when I evening. He said: Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and the evil of Satan and his association. Say it when you wake, and when you evening, and when you take your bed."
"7949","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: We had no food in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except the two black ones: dates and water."
"7950","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew from his wives. Shubah said, and I think he said: a month. So Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, came to him while he was in a room upon a mat which had marked his back. He said: O Messenger of Allah, Kisra drink in gold and silver, and you are thus. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They have had their good things hastened for them in their worldly life. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is twenty-nine, thus and thus, and he broke the thumb in the third."
"7951","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to seek refuge from the punishment of the grave, and the punishment of Hell, and the trial of the Dajjal."
"7952","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abbas al-Jurayri, who said: I heard Abu Uthman narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that hunger struck them. He said: And we were seven, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me seven dates, for each person a date."
"7953","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hashim said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Balj, Hashim said: Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym informed me, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Shall I not teach you, Hashim said: Shall I not guide you to a word from the treasure of Paradise from beneath the Throne: There is no power but with Allah. He says: My servant has submitted and surrendered."
"7954","Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, and Hashim said: Shubah narrated to us, Hashim said: Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym informed me, I heard Amr ibn Maymun, and Muhammad said: from Abu Balj, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever loves, and Hashim said: Whoever is pleased to find the taste of faith, let him love a person loving him only for Allah the Mighty and Majestic."
"7955","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I shall surely drive men from among you away from my Basin as the strange camel is driven away from the Basin."
"7956","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: An ifrit from the jinn pounced upon me last night to cut off my prayer, so Allah enabled me over him, and I gripped him, and I intended to tie him to the side of a pillar among the pillars of the mosque until you wake and all of you look at him. He said: Then I remembered the supplication of my brother Sulayman: Lord, grant me a kingdom which befits none after me. He said: So I sent him back humiliated."
"7957","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I hope, if my life is long, to meet Isa son of Maryam, upon him be peace. And if death hastens me, whoever of you meets him, convey my greeting of peace to him."
"7958","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I hope, if my life is long, to reach Isa son of Maryam, upon him be peace. And if death hastens me, whoever reaches him, convey my greeting of peace to him."
"7959","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, who said: I heard Ali ibn Zayd and Yunus ibn Ubayd narrating from Ammar, freedman of Banu Hashim, from Abu Hurayrah. As for Ali, he raised it, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and as for Yunus, he did not go beyond Abu Hurayrah, that he said about this verse: By the witness and the witnessed: he said, meaning the witness is the day of Arafah, and the promised is the Day of Resurrection."
"7960","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yunus, who said: I heard Ammar, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrating that he said about this verse: By the witness and the witnessed: he said: The witness is the day of Friday, and the witnessed is the day of Arafah, and the promised is the Day of Resurrection."
"7961","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Simak, from Malik ibn Zalim, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu al-Qasim, upon him be prayer and peace, the truthful and believed, say: The destruction of my nation, or the corruption of my nation, is heads, chiefs, young foolish ones from Quraysh."
"7962","Muhammad, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abbas al-Jushami, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A surah of the Quran of thirty verses interceded for a man until he was forgiven, and it is: Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the Kingdom."
"7963","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Num narrating. Abd Allah said: My father said: He is only Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Num, but Ghundar said thus, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of the cupper, and the earnings of the prostitute, and the price of the dog. He said: And the stud fee of the stallion. He said: And Abu Hurayrah said: This is from my own pocket."
"7964","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I was with Ali ibn Abi Talib when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to the people of Makkah with Baraah. So he said: What did you proclaim. He said: We proclaimed that none enters Paradise but a believer, and none circumambulates the House naked, and whoever had between him and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a covenant, his term or his period is to four months. Then when the four months pass, Allah is free of the polytheists and His Messenger, and no polytheist shall perform pilgrimage to this House after this year. He said: So I proclaimed until my voice became hoarse."
"7965","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I hope, if my life is long, to reach Isa son of Maryam. And if death hastens me, whoever of you reaches him, convey my greeting of peace to him."
"7966","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man proposed to a woman, meaning of the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at her, for in the eyes of the Ansar is something."
"7967","Sufyan narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, if Allah wills, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): People will soon strike, and Sufyan once said: men will strike the livers of camels seeking knowledge, finding no scholar more knowledgeable than the scholar of the people of Madinah. And people said: He is al-Umari. He said: So they put forward Malik."
"7968","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Salih, meaning Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, informing them that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When the servant of one of you suffices him the making of his food, sparing him its heat and its smoke, let him seat him with him to eat. And if he refuses, let him take a morsel and coat it, then give it to him."
"7969","He said: I read to my father Qurrah al-Zubaydi Musa ibn Tariq, from Musa, meaning Ibn Uqbah, from Abu Salih al-Samman and Ata ibn Yasar, or from one of them, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do you love to strive in supplication. Say: O Allah, help us upon thanking You, and remembering You, and good worship of You."
"7970","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is cut off by the woman, and the dog, and the donkey."
"7971","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you knew that his attending prayer with me is greater to him than a fat sheep or two sheep, he would do it. And what he attains of reward is better."
"7972","Muadh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah: A man proposed to a woman, meaning of the Ansar, so he said: Look at her, meaning that in the eyes of the Ansar is something."
"7973","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had drunk. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beat him. He said: So among us was one striking with his hand, and among us one striking with his sandal, and one striking with his garment. When he left, some of the people said: May Allah disgrace you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say thus, do not help Satan against him, but say: May Allah have mercy on you."
"7974","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid said, from Qays, who said: Abu Hurayrah stayed with us in Kufa. He said: And there was kinship between him and our freedman. Sufyan said: And he is the freedman of al-Ahmas. So Ahmas gathered. Qays said: So we came to him greeting him. And Sufyan once said: So the clan came to him. So my father said to him: O Abu Hurayrah, these are your relatives, they came to you greeting you, and you narrate to them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Welcome to them. I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three years, I was never more keen to retain hadith than I in them, until I heard him say: By Allah, for one of you to take a rope and gather firewood upon his back, then eat and give charity, is better for him than to come to a man whom Allah the Mighty and Majestic has enriched of His bounty and ask him, whether he gives him or withholds. Then he said thus with his hand: Near the Hour you will come fighting a people whose sandals are hair, as though their faces are hammered shields."
"7975","Muhammad ibn Yazid, and he is al-Wasiti, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: He says: I asked My servant for a loan and he did not lend Me, and My servant insults Me while he does not know. He says: O woe of time, O woe of time, and I am Time."
"7976","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, I know it only from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters. Dispute about the Quran is disbelief, three times. So what you know of it, act upon it, and what you are ignorant of, refer it to its knower."
"7977","Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will move his face away from the Fire by that seventy autumns."
"7978","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that he said: I never prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose prayer more resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than so-and-so. Sulayman said: He used to lengthen the first two rakahs of Zuhr, and shorten the last two, and shorten Asr, and recite in Maghrib the short Mufassal, and recite in Isha the middle Mufassal, and recite in Fajr the long Mufassal."
"7979","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have kin whom I join and they sever, and I do good to them and they do ill to me, and I forbear toward them and they are ignorant toward me. He said: If you are as you say, it is as though you feed them hot ash, and there will still be with you from Allah a supporter against them as long as you are upon that."
"7980","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he came to the graveyard and greeted the people of the graveyard. So he said: Peace upon you, abode of a believing people, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you. Then he said: I wished we had seen our brothers. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers. He said: Rather you are my companions, and my brothers are those who have not yet come, and I am their predecessor at the Basin. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you know who has not yet come of your nation. He said: What do you think, if a man had horses white-foreheaded white-legged among dark black horses, would he not know them. They said: Yes. He said: They will come on the Day of Resurrection white-foreheaded white-legged from the mark of ablution, and I am their predecessor at the Basin. Then he said: Men from among you will surely be driven away from my Basin as the stray camel is driven away. I will call them: Come. So it will be said: They changed after you. So I will say: Away, away."
"7981","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer, the believer, two or three times, feels jealousy, feels jealousy, and Allah is more intense in jealousy."
"7982","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Shall I not guide you to what Allah raises degrees with and erases sins with: many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer, and perfecting ablution upon hardships."
"7983","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Rights will surely be rendered to their people on the Day of Resurrection, until the hornless sheep is retaliated for from the horned which butted it."
"7984","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Abd Allah al-Qummi, from Hafs ibn Humayd, who said: Ziyad ibn Hudayr said: I wish I were in an enclosure of iron, with me what suffices me, neither speaking to people nor they speaking to me."
"7985","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade vows and said: It does not repel decree, and it is only extracted from the miser."
"7986","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, I heard al-Ala narrating from his father from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrates it from his Lord the Mighty and Majestic, that He said: I am the best of partners. So whoever does a deed and associates other than Me in it, I am free of him, and it is for the one he associated."
"7987","Rawh narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub narrated to us, I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Allah the Mighty and Majestic said: I am the best of partners. Whoever does a deed for Me and associates other than Me in it, I am free of him, and it is for the one he associated."
"7988","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger, the truthful and believed, Abu al-Qasim, master of the chamber, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Mercy is not stripped except from a wretched one. Shubah said: He wrote it to me, and I read it to him, meaning Mansur."
"7989","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Truffle is of manna, and its liquid is a cure for the eye. And Ajwah is of Paradise, and its liquid is a cure from poison."
"7990","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Ziyad al-Tahhan, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw a man drinking standing. So he said to him: Vomit. He said: Why. He said: Would it please you that a cat drinks with you. He said: No. He said: One worse than it has drunk with you: Satan."
"7991","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ziyad, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, and he mentioned it."
"7992","Struck through. Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Abu Zarah narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: This tribe of Quraysh will destroy my nation. They said: Then what do you command us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: If people would withdraw from them. And my father said in his illness in which he died: Strike upon this hadith, for it contradicts the hadiths from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning his saying: Listen and obey and be patient."
"7993","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he was asked about the recitation of the imam in prayer. He said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Muhammad, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: In all prayers there is recitation. So what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made audible to us, we make audible to you, and what he concealed from us, we conceal from you."
"7994","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Ukaymah al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished a prayer in which he recited aloud. So he said: Did anyone of you recite with me just now. A man said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I say, why am I contended for the Quran. He said: So the people stopped reciting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recites aloud of recitation in prayer, when they heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7995","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner has He, to Him is the kingdom and to Him is praise, and He is over everything capable, in a day one hundred times, it is for him equal to ten necks, and one hundred good deeds are written for him, and one hundred evil deeds are erased from him, and it is for him a guard from Satan that day of his until he evenings, and none comes with better than what he came with except one who did more than that."
"7996","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, in a day one hundred times, his sins are dropped even if like the foam of the sea."
"7997","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Musa, meaning Ibn Ali, from his father, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The worst in a man is anxious greed and unnerving cowardice."
"7998","Abu Amir narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Hunayn, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man reciting: Say, He is Allah, One. So he said: Incumbent. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is incumbent. He said: Paradise is incumbent for him."
"7999","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah chose from speech four: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. So whoever says: Glory be to Allah, Allah writes for him twenty good deeds, or removes from him twenty evil deeds. And whoever says: Allah is greatest, then the like of that. And whoever says: There is no god but Allah, then the like of that. And whoever says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, of his own accord, thirty good deeds are written for him, and thirty evil deeds are removed from him."
"8000","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, and Affan, Hammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Our Lord wonders at people led to Paradise in chains."
"8001","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food not from his family, he would ask about it; if it was said it was a gift, he ate, and if it was said it was charity, he said: Eat, and he did not eat."
"8002","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Men will go out from Madinah out of aversion to it, while Madinah is better for them if they only knew."
"8003","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. A man said: Supplicate Allah to make me among them. Then another stood and said: Supplicate Allah to make me among them. He said: Ukkashah has preceded you in it."
"8004","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, my father narrated to me: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sermon in which there is no testimony is like a leprous hand."
"8005","Abdullah said, and Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of Hajjaj al-Anmati, and he was trustworthy, narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, the like of it, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"8006","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank people."
"8007","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Muslim servant, or the believer, performs ablution and washes his face, every sin he looked at with his eye leaves his face with the water, or with the last drop of water, or something like this; and when he washes his hands, every sin his hands grasped leaves his hands with the water, or with the last drop of water, until he emerges pure of sins."
"8008","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik. My father said, and Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of what Allah wipes away sins with and raises ranks with? Thorough ablution despite hardships - Ishaq said: in hardships - and many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer; that is the ribat, that is the ribat, that is the ribat."
"8009","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in the call and the first row, then found no way except to draw lots for it, they would draw lots for it; and if they knew what is in early going, they would race to it; and if they knew what is in the darkness and the dawn, they would come to them even crawling."
"8010","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Ubayd, freedman of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Many an oath does not ascend to Allah in this spot; and I then saw the slave-traders in it afterwards."
"8011","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you see my qiblah here? By Allah, neither your humility nor your bowing is hidden from me; I see you from behind my back."
"8012","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muawiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from Abu Bishr, from Amir ibn Ludayn al-Ashari, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Friday is a day of festival, so do not make your festival day a day of fasting unless you fast before it or after it."
"8013","Abd al-Rahman and Abu Said said: Zaidah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which prayer is best after the obligatory? He said: Prayer in the middle of the night. It was said: Which fasting is best after Ramadan? He said: The month of Allah which you call al-Muharram."
"8014","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No weariness, nor fatigue, nor worry, nor sorrow, nor harm, nor grief befalls the believer, even the thorn he is pricked with, except Allah expiates some of his sins thereby."
"8015","Abd al-Rahman and Muammal said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us - Muammal said: al-Khurasani - Musa ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man follows the religion of his close friend, so let each of you look at whom he mixes with - and Muammal said: whom he befriends."
"8016","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do you know who the bankrupt is? They said: The bankrupt among us, O Messenger of Allah, is one who has no dirham and no goods. He said: The bankrupt of my ummah is one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with fasting and prayer and zakah, and comes having insulted the honor of this one, and slandered this one, and consumed the wealth of this one; so he is made to sit, and this one retaliates from his good deeds and this one from his good deeds; and if his good deeds are exhausted before he settles what is upon him of sins, some of their sins are taken and cast upon him, then he is cast into the Fire."
"8017","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Hasten to deeds before trials like pieces of dark night; a man wakes as a believer and sleeps as a disbeliever, and sleeps as a believer and wakes as a disbeliever; he sells his religion for a small portion of the world."
"8018","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hawshab ibn Aqil narrated to us, Mahdi narrated to me, Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Abu Hurayrah in his house and asked him about fasting the day of Arafah at Arafat. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Arafah at Arafat. My father said, and Abd al-Rahman said: from Mahdi al-Abdi."
"8019","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Khilas ibn Amr al-Hajari, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the Children of Israel, meat would not spoil and food would not go bad; and were it not for Hawwa, no female would betray her husband."
"8020","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Simak, Abdullah ibn Zalim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard my beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The corruption of my ummah is at the hands of foolish youths from Quraysh."
"8021","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Najm and prostrated, and the people prostrated with him, except two men who sought fame."
"8022","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abu Alqamah, meaning al-Farwi, narrated to us, Yazid ibn Khusayfah narrated to us, from Busr ibn Said, he said: Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No woman who has applied incense should attend the last evening prayer."
"8023","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Shutayr ibn Nahar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Good opinion is part of good worship."
"8024","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah, that Thumamah ibn Uthal, or Uthalah, embraced Islam, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take him to the garden of the sons of so-and-so and order him to wash."
"8025","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr, meaning Ibn Anas ibn Malik, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Locusts of gold were sent upon Ayyub, and he began to collect them. He said: Did I not enrich you, O Ayyub? He said: O Lord, who can be satiated of Your mercy - or he said: of Your bounty."
"8026","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There was a tree harming people on the road; a man cut it and removed it from the road, and he was admitted to Paradise for it."
"8027","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and more than one, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There was a man among those before you who never did any good except tawhid; when he was dying, he said to his family: Look, when I die, burn me until you leave me as charred coal, then grind me, then scatter me on a windy day. When he died, they did that with him, and behold he was in the grasp of Allah. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: O son of Adam, what carried you to what you did? He said: My Lord, fear of You. He said: So he was forgiven for it, though he never did any good except tawhid."
"8028","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man lying on his stomach and said: This is a lying posture Allah does not love."
"8029","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr reported to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sons of al-As are believers: Amr and Hisham."
"8030","Abu Kamil and Abu al-Nadr said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Sad al-Tai narrated to us - Abu al-Nadr said: Sad Abu Mujahid - Abu al-Mudillah, freedman of the Mother of the Believers, narrated to us: He heard Abu Hurayrah saying: We said: O Messenger of Allah, when we see you our hearts soften and we are of the people of the Hereafter, and when we leave you the world pleases us and we smell women and children. He said: If you were - or he said: If you remained in every state in the state you are in with me - the angels would shake hands with you with their palms and would visit you in your houses; and if you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin so He forgives them. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us of Paradise, what is its building? He said: A brick of gold and a brick of silver, its mortar is strong musk, its pebbles are pearl and ruby, its soil is saffron; whoever enters it enjoys and does not despair, abides and does not die; his clothes do not wear out and his youth does not perish. Three whose supplication is not rejected: the just ruler, the fasting one until he breaks fast, and the supplication of the wronged; it is carried upon the clouds, the gates of heaven are opened for it, and the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: By My might, I will aid you even after a while."
"8031","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Sad ibn Ubayd al-Tai narrated to us: I said to Zuhayr: Is he Abu al-Mujahid? He said: Yes. Abu al-Mudillah, freedman of the Mother of the Believers, narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah: We said: O Messenger of Allah, then he mentioned the hadith."
"8032","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus ibn Amr ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: I came to you last night, and nothing prevented me from entering upon you in the house you were in except that there was in the house an image of a man, and there was in the house a curtain with images; so order the head of the image to be cut so it becomes like the form of a tree, and order the curtain to be cut and made into two cushions to be trodden upon, and order the dog to be removed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did so, and behold the dog was a puppy belonging to al-Hasan and al-Husayn, peace be upon them, under a couch of theirs. He said: And he kept enjoining me with the neighbor until I thought - or saw - that he would make him an heir."
"8033","Abu Qatan and Ismail ibn Umar said: Yunus narrated to us, from Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, boasts of the people of Arafat to the angels, saying: Look at My servants unkempt and dusty."
"8034","Abu Qatan narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade foul medicine."
"8035","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled with a bridle of fire on the Day of Resurrection."
"8036","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food not from his family, he would ask about it; if it was said it was a gift, he ate, and if it was said it was charity, he said: Eat, and he did not eat."
"8037","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyyah narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to his companions while they were disputing about this tree uprooted from above the earth, having no stability. They said: We think it is the truffle. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truffle is from manna, and its water is healing for the eye; and the ajwah is from Paradise, and it is healing from poison."
"8038","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the delegation of Abd al-Qays turned back, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every man is accountable for himself; let each people make nabidh in whatever vessels seem fit to them."
"8039","He said: Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abi Talhah, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty and scarcity and humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from wronging or being wronged."
"8040","He said: Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An angel at a gate of the gates of heaven says: Who lends today will be repaid tomorrow; and an angel at another gate says: O Allah, give the spender a replacement and hasten ruin for the withholder."
"8041","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah reported to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man carried wine with him in a ship to sell it, and with him was a monkey. When the man sold wine, he mixed it with water then sold it. The monkey took the bag and climbed with it to the top of the mast, and began throwing a dinar into the sea and a dinar into the ship until he divided it."
"8042","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah - Hammam said: I found in my book from Bashir ibn Nahik, and I think only from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prayed a rakah of the dawn prayer then the sun rose, let him complete his prayer."
"8043","Bahz narrated to us, Salim, meaning Ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, Said, meaning Ibn Mina, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The breath of the fasting mouth is sweeter to Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk."
"8044","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Nahik - and I think only from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik - from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The breath of the fasting mouth is sweeter to Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk."
"8045","Bahz narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield; when one of you is fasting a day, let him not speak obscenely nor act ignorantly; and if a man insults him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting."
"8046","Abu Kamil and Affan said: Hammad narrated to us, from Abu al-Muhazzim - and Affan said: Abu al-Muhazzim reported to us - from Abu Hurayrah: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a Hajj or Umrah, and a swarm of locusts faced us - and Affan said: faced us - and we began striking them with our sticks and whips and killing them, then we felt remorse and said: What do we do being in ihram? We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: No harm in sea game."
"8047","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from Ayyub, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Ziyad ibn Riyah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever leaves the community and exits obedience and dies, his death is one of ignorance; and whoever goes out against my ummah with his sword, striking its righteous and its wicked, not sparing a believer for his faith nor fulfilling for one under covenant his covenant, he is not of my ummah; and whoever is killed under a blind banner, angering for partisanship, or fighting for partisanship, or calling to partisanship, his killing is one of ignorance."
"8048","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Euphrates will uncover a mountain of gold, and people will fight over it; ninety of every hundred will be killed - or he said: ninety-nine - each of them thinking he will be saved."
"8049","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from Ashath ibn Abdullah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A wolf came to a shepherd of sheep and took a sheep from them; the shepherd pursued it until he took it back from it. The wolf climbed a hill, sat and tucked its tail, and said: You went to a provision Allah, Mighty and Majestic, provided me and took it from me. The man said: By Allah, I have never seen like today a wolf speaking. The wolf said: More wondrous than this is a man among the date-palms between the two lava tracts informing you of what has passed and what will be after you. The man was a Jew; so the man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), embraced Islam and informed him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) believed him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a sign of the signs before the Hour; a man is about to go out and not return until his sandals and his whip inform him of what his family did after him."
"8050","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When you hear the crowing of roosters at night, they have seen an angel, so ask Allah of His bounty; and when you hear the braying of the donkey, it has seen a devil, so seek refuge in Allah from Satan."
"8051","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said, meaning al-Maqburi, narrated to me, from Abu Ubaydah, from Said ibn Yasar, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one performs ablution and perfects and completes his ablution, then comes to the mosque wanting only prayer in it, except Allah rejoices with him as the family of the absent one rejoice at his arrival."
"8052","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Muslim women, let no neighbor despise her neighbor, not even a sheep trotter."
"8053","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Said narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: There is no god but Allah alone; He strengthened His soldiers, aided His servant, defeated the confederates alone, and there is nothing after Him."
"8054","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an expedition and said: If you find so-and-so and so-and-so, two men of Quraysh, burn them with fire. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when we wanted to leave: I had ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so with fire, yet none punishes with fire except Allah, Mighty and Majestic; so if you find them, kill them."
"8055","Hashim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Irak, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The worst of people is the two-faced one, who comes to these with a face and to these with a face."
"8056","Hashim and al-Khuzai, meaning Abu Salamah, said: Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abi Salim, from Muawiyah ibn Mutib al-Hudhali, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard him saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What did your Lord return to you concerning intercession? He said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I thought you would be the first of my ummah to ask me about it, seeing your eagerness for knowledge. By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, their crowding at the gates of Paradise does not concern me as dearly as the completion of my intercession; and my intercession is for whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah sincerely, his heart confirming his tongue and his tongue his heart."
"8057","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin narrating from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None spoke in the cradle except three: Isa son of Maryam; and there was among the Children of Israel a worshipper called Jurayj, who built a cell and worshipped in it. He said: The Children of Israel one day mentioned the worship of Jurayj, and a prostitute among them said: If you wish, I will seduce him. They said: We wish. He said: She came to him and exposed herself to him, but he did not turn to her; then she gave herself to a shepherd who sheltered his sheep at the foot of the cell of Jurayj, and she became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. They said: From whom? She said: From Jurayj. They came to him, brought him down, insulted him, beat him and demolished his cell. He said: What is the matter with you? They said: You committed adultery with this prostitute and she gave birth to a boy. He said: Where is he? They said: Here he is. He said: He stood, prayed and supplicated, then turned to the boy, pierced him with his finger and said: By Allah, O boy, who is your father? He said: I am the son of the shepherd. They rushed to Jurayj, kissing him, and said: We will build your cell of gold. He said: I have no need of that; build it of clay as it was. He said: While a woman had her son in her lap nursing him, a rider of fine appearance passed by her, and she said: O Allah, make my son like this. He said: He left her breast and turned to the rider and said: O Allah, do not make me like him. He said: Then he returned to her breast sucking it. Abu Hurayrah said: It is as if I look at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating to me the act of the boy and placing his finger in his mouth, sucking it. Then a slave-girl being beaten was passed by, and she said: O Allah, do not make my son like her. He said: He left her breast, turned to his mother and said: O Allah, make me like her. He said: That is when they repeated the speech, and she said: May you be bereaved, a rider of fine appearance passed, and I said: O Allah, make my son like him, and you said: O Allah, do not make me like him; and this slave-girl was passed by, and I said: O Allah, do not make my son like her, and you said: O Allah, make me like her. He said: O mother, the rider of fine appearance is a tyrant of the tyrants, and this slave-girl, they say: She stole though she did not steal, and committed adultery though she did not commit adultery, while she says: Allah suffices me."
"8058","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None spoke in the cradle except three: Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon him, and a boy in the time of Jurayj, and another boy, then he mentioned the hadith. He said: As for Jurayj, he was a worshipper among the Children of Israel, and he had a mother; one day he was praying when his mother longed for him and said: O Jurayj. He said: O Lord, is prayer better or my mother - shall I come to her? Then he prayed, and she called him and he said the like of that, then she called him and he said the like of that and prayed. It weighed upon his mother, and she said: O Allah, show Jurayj the prostitutes. Then he ascended a cell of his, and there was an adulteress of the Children of Israel, then he mentioned something like it."
"8059","Abu Amir narrated to us, Aflah ibn Said, a shaykh of the people of Quba of the Ansar, narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Rafi, freedman of Umm Salamah, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If you live long, you will soon see people going out in the wrath of Allah and returning in His curse, in their hands like the tails of cows."
"8060","Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Jafar, meaning Ibn Burqan, narrated to us, he said: I heard Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not fear poverty for you, but I fear rivalry in abundance for you; and I do not fear mistake for you, but I fear deliberate sin for you."
"8061","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated to us, Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sarh reported to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood addressing the people and mentioned faith in Allah and struggle in the path of Allah among the best deeds to Allah. He said: A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I am killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating - will Allah expiate my sins? He said: Yes. He said: How did you say? He repeated the question as he said it. He said: Yes. He said: How did you say? He repeated the question also. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I am killed in the path of Allah, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating - will Allah expiate my sins? He said: Yes, except debt, for Jibril, peace be upon him, whispered that to me."
"8062","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in prayer, speaking aloud and silently; so we spoke aloud in what he spoke aloud in, and silently in what he was silent in. I heard him saying: There is no prayer except with recitation."
"8063","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you performs ablution, let him blow water from his nose, and when he cleanses with stones, let him do an odd number."
"8064","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one who breaks his ablution is not accepted until he performs ablution. He said: A man of the people of Hadramawt said to him: What is breaking ablution, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: Breaking wind, loud or silent."
"8065","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, that Jibril, peace be upon him, came and greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recognized his voice and said: Enter. He said: In the house is a curtain on the wall with images; cut off their heads and make them a carpet or cushions to be trodden; for we do not enter a house with images."
"8066","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: While the Abyssinians were playing with their spears before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Umar entered and reached for the pebbles to pelt them with them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Leave them, O Umar."
"8067","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Jafar al-Jazari, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If religion were at the Pleiades, a man of Persia, or of the sons of Persia, would go until he attains it."
"8068","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from Jafar al-Jazari, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you did not sin, Allah would take you away and bring a people who sin then seek forgiveness from Allah, and He forgives them."
"8069","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, and Abd al-Ala, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so oppose them. Abd al-Razzaq said in his hadith: al-Zuhri said: And the command of dyes - the blackest is most beloved to us. Mamar said: And al-Zuhri used to dye black."
"8070","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I know only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Surplus water is not withheld to withhold thereby surplus pasture."
"8071","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Kumayl ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among date-palms of some people of Madinah, and he said: O Abu Hurayrah, ruined are the abundant, except one who says thus and thus and thus - three times - scattering with his palm to his right and to his left and before him; and few are they. Then he walked a while and said: O Abu Hurayrah, shall I not guide you to a treasure of the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: There is no power nor strength except in Allah, and no refuge from Allah except to Him. Then he walked a while and said: O Abu Hurayrah, do you know what is the right of people upon Allah and what is the right of Allah upon people? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah upon people is to worship Him and not associate anything with Him; and when they do that, it is right upon Him not to punish them."
"8072","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, freedman of Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should wish for death: either a doer of good, increasing in goodness, or a doer of evil, perhaps seeking to make amends."
"8073","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears and says in his oath: By al-Lat, let him say: There is no god but Allah; and whoever says to his companion: Come, let me gamble with you, let him give charity."
"8074","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears and says: If Allah wills, he has not broken his oath. Abd al-Razzaq said, and he abridged it, meaning Mamar."
"8075","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj reported to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yuhannis reported to me, from Abu Abdullah al-Qarraz, that he said: I bear witness - three - upon Abu Hurayrah that he said: Abu al-Qasim said: Whoever intends the people of this town with evil - meaning the people of Madinah - Allah melts him as salt melts in water."
"8076","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the day of Khaybar, and he said - meaning of a man claiming Islam: This is of the people of the Fire. When we attended the fighting, the man fought fiercely and was wounded. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the man of whom you said he is of the people of the Fire fought fiercely today and has died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To the Fire. Some people almost doubted. While they were in that, it was said: He has not died, but he has severe wounds. When night came, he could not endure the wounds and killed himself. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of that and said: Allah is greatest; I bear witness that I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then he ordered Bilal to call among the people that none enters Paradise except a Muslim soul, and that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, supports this religion with the wicked man."
"8077","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb reported to us, from al-Zuhri, Ibn al-Musayyab reported to me that Abu Hurayrah said: We witnessed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Khaybar, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of a man among those with him professing Islam: This is of the people of the Fire, then he mentioned its meaning, except he said: It weighed upon some of the Muslims, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has confirmed your speech; so-and-so has killed himself."
"8078","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you count the martyr among you? They said: One killed in the path of Allah. He said: The martyrs of my ummah then are few: Killing in the path of Allah is martyrdom, the belly is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, the woman dying in childbirth is martyrdom, and the plague is martyrdom."
"8079","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil reported to us, from Abu Sinan, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chose from speech four: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. He said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, twenty good deeds are written for him for it and twenty sins are removed from him; and whoever says: Allah is greatest, the like of that; and whoever says: There is no god but Allah, the like of that; and whoever says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, from himself, thirty good deeds are written for him for it and thirty sins are removed from him for it."
"8080","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: At the end of time, Dhu al-Suwayqatayn will appear against the Kabah. He said: I thought he said: And he destroys it."
"8081","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Jafar, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Abu Tariq, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who of my ummah will take five traits to act upon them or teach them to one who acts upon them? He said: I said: I, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He took my hand and counted them in it, then said: Fear the prohibitions, you will be the most worshipful of people; be content with what Allah apportioned for you, you will be the richest of people; do good to your neighbor, you will be a believer; love for people what you love for yourself, you will be a Muslim; and do not laugh much, for much laughter kills the heart."
"8082","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amr ibn Abi Sufyan al-Thaqafi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a scouting party and put over them Asim ibn Thabit, grandfather of Asim ibn Umar. They went until, at part of the road between Usfan and Makkah where they stopped, they were mentioned to a clan of Hudhayl called Banu Lihyan. They followed them with nearly a hundred archers, tracking their traces until they stopped at a stopping place they had stopped at and found date-stones they had provisioned from the dates of Madinah, and said: This is of the dates of Yathrib. They followed their traces until they caught them. When Asim ibn Thabit and his companions sensed them, they took refuge on a hill, and the people came and surrounded them, saying: You have covenant and pledge, if you come down to us, that we will not kill any of you. Asim ibn Thabit said: As for me, I will not come down under the protection of a disbeliever; O Allah, inform Your Messenger of us. He said: They fought them and shot them and killed Asim among seven men, and Khubayb ibn Adi and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah and another man remained. They gave them covenant and pledge, if they came down to them. When they gained power over them, they loosened the strings of their bows and tied them with them. The third man with them said: This is the first treachery. He refused to accompany them; they dragged him, but he refused to follow them, so they struck his neck. They went with Khubayb ibn Adi and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah until they sold them in Makkah. The sons of al-Harith ibn Amir ibn Nawfal bought Khubayb, and he had killed al-Harith on the day of Badr. He remained with them captive until, when they agreed to kill him, he borrowed a razor from one of the daughters of al-Harith to shave with it, and she lent him. She said: I was heedless of a boy of mine, and he walked to him until he came to him. She said: He took him and placed him on his thigh, and when I saw him I was frightened with a fright he recognized, with the razor in his hand, and said: Do you fear I will kill him? I would not do so, if Allah wills. She said: And she used to say: I never saw a captive better than Khubayb; I saw him eating of a bunch of grapes when there was no fruit in Makkah that day, though he was bound in iron; it was only a provision Allah provided him. She said: Then they took him out of the sanctuary to kill him, and he said: Leave me to pray two rakahs. He prayed two rakahs and said: Were it not that you think I am afraid of death, I would increase. He was the first to institute the two rakahs at killing. Then he said: O Allah, count them in number. I do not care when I am killed a Muslim, on which side my death for Allah is; that is for the sake of God, and if He wills He blesses the limbs of a torn body. Then Uqbah ibn al-Harith stood to him and killed him. Quraysh sent to Asim to be given something of his body by which they would recognize him, and he had killed a great one of their great ones on the day of Badr; so Allah sent upon him like a cloud of hornets that protected him from their messengers, and they could not take anything of him."
"8083","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not accompany a company with a dog or a bell."
"8084","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child of adultery is the worst of the three."
"8085","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ayyub, meaning Ibn Utbah, narrated to us, Abu Kathir al-Suhaymi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have choice in their sale until they part, or their sale is with choice."
"8086","Hashim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Kathir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man should outbid the sale of his brother, nor propose over his engagement, nor should a woman stipulate the divorce of her sister to empty her bowl; for she has only what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, decreed for her."
"8087","Hashim Abu al-Nadr said: al-Faraj, meaning Ibn Fudalah, narrated to us, Abu Sad al-Himsi narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Supplications I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I will not leave them as long as I live: I heard him saying: O Allah, make me magnify gratitude to You, increase remembrance of You, follow Your counsel and keep Your bequest."
"8088","Hashim narrated to us, al-Faraj ibn Fudalah narrated to us, Ali ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Why is Friday named? He said: Because in it the clay of your father Adam was formed, and in it is the swoon and the resurrection, and in it is the assault; and in the last three hours of it is an hour in which whoever supplicates Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is answered."
"8089","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Abu Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he does not wrong him, nor abandon him, nor despise him; enough evil for a man to despise his Muslim brother."
"8090","Yahya ibn Adam and Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us - the meaning, and the wording is the wording of Yahya ibn Adam - they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the lavatory, and I brought him a vessel with water; he cleaned himself, then wiped his hand on the ground, then washed it; then I brought him another vessel and he performed ablution with it. My father said: Aswad, meaning Shadhan, said in this hadith: When he entered the lavatory, I brought him water in a vessel or in a water-skin, and he mentioned it with its isnad."
"8091","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me with three and forbade me three: He ordered me with the two rakahs of Duha every day, and witr before sleep, and fasting three days of every month; and he forbade me pecking like the pecking of the rooster, and squatting like the squatting of the dog, and turning like the turning of the fox."
"8092","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn Mawhab, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he raised it, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant."
"8093","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For one of you to sit upon an ember that burns his clothes until it reaches his skin is better for him than to sit upon a grave."
"8094","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nakhai, from Abu Zurah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever names himself with my name should not take my kunyah, and whoever takes my kunyah should not name himself with my name."
"8095","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying, Mighty and Majestic: Enter the gate prostrating, he said: They entered crawling, and: Say: Hittah, he said: They changed and said: Wheat, in a hair."
"8096","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A good word is charity, and every step he walks to prayer - or he said: to the mosque - is charity."
"8097","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he called war deception."
"8098","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning al-Khadir, he said: He was named Khadir only because he sat upon a white fleece, and behold it shook green beneath him."
"8099","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, Said ibn Saman narrated to me: I heard Abu Hurayrah narrating to Abu Qatadah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allegiance will be given to a man between the Corner and the Maqam, and only its own people will violate the House; and when they violate it, do not ask about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Abyssinians will come and destroy it, a ruin never inhabited after it; they are those who will extract its treasure."
